1
00:00:00,462 --> 00:00:02,821
[Hidden deep in every corner of the vast island]

2
00:00:03,465 --> 00:00:05,772
[Find and decode the ancient language]

3
00:00:05,772 --> 00:00:08,242
[There can only be two princes]
The prince status will only be given to two.

4
00:00:08,242 --> 00:00:09,269
Is it "CARAMEL"?

5
00:00:09,269 --> 00:00:11,040
[The owners of the throne are revealed]
I was searching for ages!

6
00:00:11,040 --> 00:00:12,579
Oh, I got it.

7
00:00:12,579 --> 00:00:15,883
[Shin Dong & Johnny rise as princes]
I'm the prince!

8
00:00:15,883 --> 00:00:18,051
[And the four left behind are paupers?!]
No! I'm the pauper!

9
00:00:18,619 --> 00:00:20,257
[The game isn't over yet]
Time for an urgent announcement!

10
00:00:20,257 --> 00:00:21,466
Through some games,

11
00:00:21,466 --> 00:00:23,257
you'll get a chance
for a status upgrade today!

12
00:00:23,257 --> 00:00:24,191
That's a good announcement!

13
00:00:24,191 --> 00:00:26,180
[The real final chance for
these guys to upgrade their status]

14
00:00:26,180 --> 00:00:29,516
[Only the winners will become commoners]

15
00:00:30,084 --> 00:00:32,811
[Their competitiveness explodes]

16
00:00:32,811 --> 00:00:34,021
Please…!

17
00:00:34,468 --> 00:00:35,602
[Finally escaped his pauper status!]

18
00:00:35,602 --> 00:00:37,365
Ji Sung gets a status upgrade!

19
00:00:39,067 --> 00:00:41,820
[And soon]
DAWN gets a status upgrade!

20
00:00:42,195 --> 00:00:44,756
[Dinner time for the two princes,
the two commoners, and the two paupers]

21
00:00:45,239 --> 00:00:49,119
[The brutal status-based dinner
strikes again today]

22
00:00:49,616 --> 00:00:51,451
Why does this taste so good?

23
00:00:51,451 --> 00:00:53,954
[+The commoners are invited too]
[A final feast for the princes]

24
00:00:53,954 --> 00:00:55,117
[Agony]
Ugh! It looks so delicious!!!

25
00:00:55,117 --> 00:00:56,356
I want pizza so much right now…

26
00:00:56,356 --> 00:00:57,958
Can we just dip it in the sauce?

27
00:00:57,958 --> 00:00:59,560
[The paupers even resort to begging]
Can we please just dip it in the sauce?

28
00:00:59,560 --> 00:01:00,894
Oh!! It fell!!

29
00:01:00,894 --> 00:01:02,696
[Literally a pie in the sky for the paupers]
It fell!! It fell!!

30
00:01:02,696 --> 00:01:03,730
Oh, why?

31
00:01:03,730 --> 00:01:04,973
[Wait, don't we have ramyeon?!]
There's ramyeon left!

32
00:01:04,973 --> 00:01:05,832
Oh, there's ramyeon!!

33
00:01:05,832 --> 00:01:07,285
We can eat ramyeon in the tent, right?

34
00:01:07,285 --> 00:01:08,569
[But]
A serious incident has happened.

35
00:01:08,569 --> 00:01:10,070
[Their precious ramyeon has gone missing?!]
A Bowl Noodle Soup theft!

36
00:01:10,070 --> 00:01:11,738
- What are you talking about?
- Who is it?

37
00:01:11,738 --> 00:01:14,945
- If you get caught, there's no mercy.
- They said it's someone in here!

38
00:01:14,945 --> 00:01:19,283
[The real culprit
who stole the ramyeon is among us]

39
00:01:19,815 --> 00:01:20,857
[Lee Teuk]

40
00:01:21,350 --> 00:01:22,501
[Shin Dong]

41
00:01:22,501 --> 00:01:23,568
[DAWN]

42
00:01:23,568 --> 00:01:25,045
[Johnny]

43
00:01:25,045 --> 00:01:26,321
[Kim Yo Han]

44
00:01:26,321 --> 00:01:27,298
[Ji Sung]

45
00:01:35,796 --> 00:01:37,865
- Everyone, there's ramyeon left!
- Oh, right!

46
00:01:37,865 --> 00:01:39,333
- Oh, there's ramyeon!!
- That's true!

47
00:01:39,333 --> 00:01:41,068
[Super excited that there's ramyeon left]
We can eat ramyeon in the tent, right?

48
00:01:41,068 --> 00:01:42,797
Even if we eat it now…

49
00:01:42,797 --> 00:01:46,227
Don't bring that out yet!
They're all gonna eat it!

50
00:01:46,227 --> 00:01:47,828
We were gonna eat that later
just by ourselves!

51
00:01:47,828 --> 00:01:49,576
The production team
seriously can't read the room!

52
00:01:49,576 --> 00:01:50,811
[Cluelessly brought all the remaining ramyeon]

53
00:01:50,811 --> 00:01:51,958
[+Kimchi]
Alright, the remaining…

54
00:01:51,958 --> 00:01:54,014
Oh, Kimchi!!!!

55
00:01:54,014 --> 00:01:56,886
Take it out later!
We're gonna eat it in our tent!

56
00:01:58,552 --> 00:02:01,021
[Merciful princes]
We'll give you a chance to eat it in the tent.

57
00:02:01,021 --> 00:02:02,689
- We won't eat it.
- Oh, you're not eating it?

58
00:02:02,689 --> 00:02:03,824
- Thank you.
- Enjoy it in the tent.

59
00:02:03,824 --> 00:02:04,636
Thank you.

60
00:02:04,636 --> 00:02:05,638
[Snapped back to reality]
But…

61
00:02:05,638 --> 00:02:06,727
We brought the remaining cups of ramyeon.

62
00:02:06,727 --> 00:02:07,894
Didn't you say there was Cup Ramyeon?

63
00:02:07,894 --> 00:02:08,829
Yeah! The Bowl Noodle Soup.

64
00:02:08,829 --> 00:02:10,764
We packed the Cup Ramyeon...

65
00:02:10,764 --> 00:02:13,133
- But the Cup Ramyeon's gone!
- What?!

66
00:02:13,133 --> 00:02:14,262
- It must've been the wind.
- Who did it?

67
00:02:14,262 --> 00:02:15,555
- Who did it?
- Someone must've taken it.

68
00:02:15,555 --> 00:02:16,637
Who ate it...?

69
00:02:16,637 --> 00:02:19,273
A serious incident has happened.

70
00:02:19,273 --> 00:02:20,760
A Cup Ramyeon theft!

71
00:02:20,760 --> 00:02:22,242
- Who is it?
- Seriously?

72
00:02:22,242 --> 00:02:23,443
Lee Teuk.

73
00:02:23,443 --> 00:02:25,312
[The culprit within us!]
Ugh, Lee Teuk! Seriously!

74
00:02:25,312 --> 00:02:27,548
- If you get caught, there's no mercy.
- It's someone here.

75
00:02:27,548 --> 00:02:29,440
[Suspect 1. Lee Teuk]
Wait a sec, Lee Teuk!

76
00:02:29,440 --> 00:02:30,717
Wow, Lee Teuk, you ate it?

77
00:02:30,717 --> 00:02:32,534
- Wow, this is legendary.
- During break time,

78
00:02:32,534 --> 00:02:34,457
(Suspicious)
did you eat it? Be honest.

79
00:02:34,457 --> 00:02:37,464
I'm literally skin and bones right now.
What could I have eaten?

80
00:02:37,464 --> 00:02:39,059
This guy ate it!

81
00:02:39,059 --> 00:02:40,828
[Wronged]
I seriously didn't eat it.

82
00:02:40,828 --> 00:02:42,274
He ate it for sure.

83
00:02:42,274 --> 00:02:43,776
You're the one who ate it!

84
00:02:43,776 --> 00:02:45,132
Lee Teuk, did you eat it?

85
00:02:45,132 --> 00:02:46,695
You're full right now, aren't you?

86
00:02:46,695 --> 00:02:47,921
I'm full.

87
00:02:47,921 --> 00:02:48,997
You ate it!!!

88
00:02:48,997 --> 00:02:50,103
[Suspect 2. Shin Dong]
Shin Dong, did you eat the Bowl Noodle Soup?

89
00:02:50,103 --> 00:02:52,409
I didn't eat it. I don't like ramyeon.

90
00:02:52,409 --> 00:02:53,660
[Witness]
Shin Dong has been saying that!

91
00:02:53,660 --> 00:02:54,620
I don't like ramyeon.

92
00:02:54,620 --> 00:02:55,830
[A battle of suspicions]
Shin Dong ate it.

93
00:02:55,830 --> 00:02:57,248
- I didn't eat it, for real.
- Look, look.

94
00:02:57,248 --> 00:02:58,374
[Suspicious]
Lee Teuk, why are you accusing him?

95
00:02:58,374 --> 00:03:00,016
No, look…!

96
00:03:00,016 --> 00:03:02,336
DAWN definitely didn't eat anything!

97
00:03:02,336 --> 00:03:03,684
- He's eating now because he's hungry.
- Of course.

98
00:03:03,684 --> 00:03:04,651
[Ji Sung is also ruled out]
Ji Sung didn't eat it either.

99
00:03:04,651 --> 00:03:06,553
How could I eat this
after having ramyeon?

100
00:03:06,553 --> 00:03:08,633
The culprit is one of the princes!

101
00:03:08,633 --> 00:03:10,257
No!

102
00:03:10,257 --> 00:03:11,845
- The culprit is…
- Either Shin Dong or Johnny.

103
00:03:11,845 --> 00:03:14,181
[Is Shin Dong or Johnny the culprit?]
Seeing how he's framing us…

104
00:03:14,181 --> 00:03:15,332
Because…

105
00:03:15,332 --> 00:03:18,360
the younger guys wouldn't
even dare dream of doing that.

106
00:03:18,360 --> 00:03:19,305
- That's true.
- Yeah.

107
00:03:19,305 --> 00:03:20,442
They wouldn't even dare think about it.

108
00:03:20,442 --> 00:03:23,537
Honestly, it's gotta be
either Shin Dong or Lee Teuk.

109
00:03:23,537 --> 00:03:25,067
Should we play a round of Mafia with this setup?

110
00:03:25,067 --> 00:03:25,859
- Shall we do it?
- For real?

111
00:03:25,859 --> 00:03:26,860
It's you, huh?

112
00:03:26,860 --> 00:03:27,875
Johnny!

113
00:03:27,875 --> 00:03:30,781
I'm way younger than you.
How could I even mess with that?

114
00:03:30,781 --> 00:03:32,779
That's pretty suspicious, though?

115
00:03:32,779 --> 00:03:34,618
[Great acting or actually innocent…?]

116
00:03:34,618 --> 00:03:37,321
Hey, let's not play dirty
over something like this.

117
00:03:37,321 --> 00:03:38,455
Ji Sung, is it you?

118
00:03:38,455 --> 00:03:39,831
I don't really like
that ramyeon much.

119
00:03:39,831 --> 00:03:41,793
[Right?]
I like the Omori ramyeon.

120
00:03:41,793 --> 00:03:44,461
If it's one of the princes,

121
00:03:44,461 --> 00:03:46,129
let's strip them of their prince title!

122
00:03:46,129 --> 00:03:47,673
What if it's one of the paupers?

123
00:03:47,673 --> 00:03:49,730
[That's a sharp question]

124
00:03:49,730 --> 00:03:51,858
Sleep without a tent?

125
00:03:51,858 --> 00:03:54,268
I can't sleep without a tent…

126
00:03:54,268 --> 00:03:57,171
Lee Teuk ate it!
He said he can't sleep without a tent.

127
00:03:57,171 --> 00:03:58,305
[Closing in on the suspect…?]
Oh, seriously, here…

128
00:03:58,305 --> 00:04:01,008
- You end up getting caught over things like this.
- No, it's not me!

129
00:04:01,008 --> 00:04:03,043
["If I'm the culprit…?" Pledge announcement!]
Then say, "If it's really me,"

130
00:04:03,043 --> 00:04:04,356
and each make a pledge.

131
00:04:04,356 --> 00:04:07,147
- If I ate it…!
- If I ate it…?

132
00:04:07,147 --> 00:04:09,516
- What are you willing to stake?
- Exactly!

133
00:04:09,516 --> 00:04:10,717
I'll go last!

134
00:04:10,717 --> 00:04:12,315
[Shin Dong makes his pledge first]
I'll go first.

135
00:04:12,315 --> 00:04:14,555
If I ate the Bowl Noodle Soup,

136
00:04:14,555 --> 00:04:15,489
on the flight back to Korea,

137
00:04:15,489 --> 00:04:17,559
[For the flight home: Giving up business class]
I'll give up my business class seat completely.

138
00:04:17,559 --> 00:04:18,692
I'll fly economy.

139
00:04:18,692 --> 00:04:20,427
Huh? He's being for real then.

140
00:04:20,427 --> 00:04:22,727
Shin Dong finds the seats super uncomfortable.

141
00:04:22,727 --> 00:04:24,362
You can trust me with this, right?

142
00:04:24,362 --> 00:04:26,587
I know Shin Dong well,
so the fact that he's saying that…

143
00:04:26,587 --> 00:04:28,213
Okay, DAWN.

144
00:04:28,213 --> 00:04:31,341
[DAWN's pledge is?]
Wow, this is really… But that was a strong one.

145
00:04:31,772 --> 00:04:34,207
If I ate that Cup Ramyeon...!

146
00:04:34,207 --> 00:04:35,553
If you ate it?

147
00:04:35,553 --> 00:04:37,514
First, that just doesn't make any sense.

148
00:04:37,514 --> 00:04:39,641
- And?
- What?

149
00:04:39,641 --> 00:04:40,909
- Huh?
- No, I mean, I…

150
00:04:40,909 --> 00:04:42,816
Hey, was it you?

151
00:04:42,816 --> 00:04:44,115
[Wow, is it unexpectedly DAWN?]
Is it surprisingly him?

152
00:04:44,115 --> 00:04:46,317
Come on, Shin Dong. If I ate the ramyeon,

153
00:04:46,317 --> 00:04:47,831
would I have eaten this much food?

154
00:04:47,831 --> 00:04:49,942
You've been eating a lot lately.

155
00:04:49,942 --> 00:04:52,382
He kept eating so we wouldn't suspect him!

156
00:04:52,382 --> 00:04:54,528
- Was it you?
- Really?

157
00:04:54,528 --> 00:04:58,498
[Playing the broke card]
I've got nothing to bet.

158
00:04:58,498 --> 00:05:00,033
- If I ate it…!
- Yeah?

159
00:05:00,033 --> 00:05:02,970
This TABASCO sauce…

160
00:05:02,970 --> 00:05:05,514
I'll pour it into a soju glass and down it!

161
00:05:06,360 --> 00:05:07,443
I think anyone could do that.

162
00:05:07,443 --> 00:05:09,576
[That's a weak pledge]
You could just drink that.

163
00:05:09,576 --> 00:05:11,144
If I drink that wrong,
I could literally die.

164
00:05:11,144 --> 00:05:12,491
Okay, Yo Han.

165
00:05:12,491 --> 00:05:14,451
Firstly, I didn't eat it!

166
00:05:14,451 --> 00:05:16,535
If I ate it…!

167
00:05:16,535 --> 00:05:18,204
I have to sleep
in the tent tonight, right?

168
00:05:18,204 --> 00:05:20,499
I'll sleep outside the tent,
wrapped in a sleeping bag!

169
00:05:20,499 --> 00:05:22,322
Sleeping outdoors.

170
00:05:22,322 --> 00:05:23,836
[Yo Han's pledge: Sleep outside the tent]
Sleeping outside the tent?

171
00:05:23,836 --> 00:05:25,092
- Yes, yes.
- Okay!

172
00:05:25,092 --> 00:05:26,380
Yo Han, don't you like that kind of thing?

173
00:05:26,380 --> 00:05:27,506
I don't like it.

174
00:05:27,506 --> 00:05:28,524
I like beds too.

175
00:05:28,524 --> 00:05:30,842
- Oh, really???
- Johnny.

176
00:05:30,842 --> 00:05:32,833
- If it's me…
- Yeah.

177
00:05:32,833 --> 00:05:35,435
I'll take a quick dip in the Red Sea!

178
00:05:35,435 --> 00:05:36,436
[Right now?]

179
00:05:36,436 --> 00:05:37,529
Like right now?

180
00:05:37,529 --> 00:05:38,639
[I'll run to the Red Sea right now]
I'll run there now!

181
00:05:38,639 --> 00:05:39,465
- For real?
- For real.

182
00:05:39,465 --> 00:05:41,008
That was gonna be my pledge…

183
00:05:41,008 --> 00:05:42,910
[Ji Sung's turn]
Okay! Ji Sung.

184
00:05:42,910 --> 00:05:44,122
[Wow…]

185
00:05:44,122 --> 00:05:46,250
If I am the culprit...

186
00:05:46,691 --> 00:05:48,608
[Ssp…]

187
00:05:49,349 --> 00:05:52,287
- Was it you?
- Ji Sung's already acting shady.

188
00:05:53,282 --> 00:05:54,388
[Slap]

189
00:05:54,388 --> 00:05:56,256
[Fiddling]
Ji Sung, it's all okay.

190
00:05:56,256 --> 00:05:57,990
But I guess when
you can't think of a pledge,

191
00:05:57,990 --> 00:05:59,658
everyone reaches for the hot sauce.

192
00:06:01,295 --> 00:06:02,229
Then!

193
00:06:02,229 --> 00:06:04,231
I'll just take this pasta,

194
00:06:04,231 --> 00:06:05,832
[Mix the pasta with hot sauce and eat it?]
mix this in and eat all of it?

195
00:06:05,832 --> 00:06:08,742
- That sounds so good!
- Seriously, hot sauce!

196
00:06:08,742 --> 00:06:10,595
If you ate the Cup Ramyeon,

197
00:06:10,595 --> 00:06:12,052
can you become a pauper?!

198
00:06:13,073 --> 00:06:14,614
I can't…

199
00:06:14,614 --> 00:06:16,443
- Huh?
- Oh, if I ate it…

200
00:06:16,443 --> 00:06:17,878
If… If I ate it…

201
00:06:17,878 --> 00:06:18,890
I didn't eat it, so...

202
00:06:18,890 --> 00:06:20,280
It's you, huh?

203
00:06:20,280 --> 00:06:22,320
[Stammering]
The Cup Ramyeon... As a commoner…

204
00:06:22,320 --> 00:06:24,251
What are you even talking about right now?

205
00:06:24,251 --> 00:06:26,522
- Oh, but, like…
- Ji Sung's bad at lying!

206
00:06:26,522 --> 00:06:29,274
But pauper… I mean, doesn't it mean
I don't become a pauper?

207
00:06:29,274 --> 00:06:31,291
No. It means you will become a pauper.

208
00:06:31,291 --> 00:06:34,030
- If you ate the Bowl Noodle Soup…
- That means you become a pauper.

209
00:06:34,030 --> 00:06:36,030
[The paupers]
Then 3 people will sleep in the tent.

210
00:06:36,030 --> 00:06:38,222
Can you become a pauper?
If you ate it?

211
00:06:38,222 --> 00:06:39,266
Oh, I can't.

212
00:06:39,266 --> 00:06:41,120
I don't want to be a pauper.

213
00:06:41,120 --> 00:06:43,898
- Then that means you ate it!
- Then that means you ate it!

214
00:06:43,898 --> 00:06:45,239
How did it get like this?

215
00:06:45,239 --> 00:06:47,289
- If you didn't eat it, you don't become a pauper.
- If you did, you can't bet on it.

216
00:06:47,289 --> 00:06:49,376
If you ate it, you become a pauper.

217
00:06:49,376 --> 00:06:50,655
[Ji Sung, was it you?]
Oh, was it you?

218
00:06:50,655 --> 00:06:53,380
[Caught the ramyeon thief]

219
00:06:53,380 --> 00:06:54,915
[Everyone except the culprit stands up]
Hey, was it you?

220
00:06:54,915 --> 00:06:57,184
- Wow! Who is this guy?
- Wow, seriously!

221
00:06:57,184 --> 00:06:58,452
Hey!

222
00:06:58,452 --> 00:06:59,471
- Hey!
- Hey, Ji Sung!

223
00:06:59,471 --> 00:07:00,915
It wasn't even your team's ramyeon!

224
00:07:00,915 --> 00:07:03,056
It was our team's!

225
00:07:03,056 --> 00:07:04,892
- What's up with this guy?
- Seriously!

226
00:07:04,892 --> 00:07:06,295
[Stayed quiet all this time to act up at the end]
Hey, that Bowl Noodle Soup was mine!

227
00:07:06,295 --> 00:07:08,022
- Wait a second!
- What's up with this guy?

228
00:07:08,022 --> 00:07:09,340
You have such an innocent face,

229
00:07:09,340 --> 00:07:11,064
[Slurping ramyeon from behind]
but behind our backs...

230
00:07:11,064 --> 00:07:12,432
I didn't eat it...

231
00:07:12,432 --> 00:07:14,134
[It's too late now, Ji Sung]
What do you mean you didn't eat it? It's over!

232
00:07:14,134 --> 00:07:14,935
Ji Sung!

233
00:07:14,935 --> 00:07:16,904
[Tear drop…]
Hey, what's up with this guy?

234
00:07:16,904 --> 00:07:17,974
Hey, who are you?

235
00:07:17,974 --> 00:07:19,549
- Were you really this kind of person?
- Betrayal!

236
00:07:19,549 --> 00:07:20,807
Is this who you really are?

237
00:07:20,807 --> 00:07:22,843
Are you pulling
the hermit crab move right now?

238
00:07:22,843 --> 00:07:24,371
Just be honest with us.

239
00:07:24,371 --> 00:07:26,388
[Confess the truth]
If you ate it, you can just say you did.

240
00:07:28,515 --> 00:07:31,360
I ate it.

241
00:07:31,952 --> 00:07:34,438
[What is happening
all of a sudden…]

242
00:07:34,438 --> 00:07:36,300
Wait, what's this about?

243
00:07:36,300 --> 00:07:38,202
I'm really flustered…

244
00:07:38,202 --> 00:07:39,787
Didn't someone say that earlier?

245
00:07:39,787 --> 00:07:42,415
- The younger guys wouldn't dare to do it?
- I…

246
00:07:42,415 --> 00:07:45,084
- I definitely wouldn't!
- Hey, what have you been teaching him?

247
00:07:45,084 --> 00:07:47,000
[He's the youngest]
I messed up.

248
00:07:47,000 --> 00:07:48,620
- You're seriously hilarious.
- This is unbelievable.

249
00:07:48,620 --> 00:07:50,938
I automatically assumed
it was one of the SUPER JUNIOR members.

250
00:07:50,938 --> 00:07:52,372
- For real!
- I was sure it was Lee Teuk!

251
00:07:52,372 --> 00:07:54,067
[Fired up]
Hey, why are you suspecting me?

252
00:07:54,067 --> 00:07:55,909
- Lee Teuk really likes ramyeon.
- That's just been your track record so far!

253
00:07:55,909 --> 00:07:58,579
I like ramyeon, but I don't steal things!

254
00:07:58,579 --> 00:08:02,850
But if you ate it, you would've eaten
something else, not the Cup Ramyeon.

255
00:08:02,850 --> 00:08:04,852
- No wonder he came out wearing a beanie.
- I know, right?

256
00:08:04,852 --> 00:08:07,254
[Metaphor for a culprit]
I guess Ji Sung really wanted to win.

257
00:08:07,254 --> 00:08:09,756
- He wanted to eat, get energy, and win.
- It's okay. It's okay with Ji Sung.

258
00:08:09,756 --> 00:08:11,783
[WANGGEOZ group toast]
Alright, let's raise our glasses together.

259
00:08:11,783 --> 00:08:12,926
Congrats, Ji Sung.

260
00:08:12,926 --> 00:08:14,505
- Hold on, hold on.
- What's going on?

261
00:08:14,505 --> 00:08:15,996
- What's this?
- Among us…

262
00:08:15,996 --> 00:08:18,993
- Yeah, among us?
- There's one more mafia member!

263
00:08:18,993 --> 00:08:20,367
Someone else ate with you?

264
00:08:20,367 --> 00:08:23,103
It's Johnny!

265
00:08:23,103 --> 00:08:24,671
You two were together!

266
00:08:24,671 --> 00:08:27,040
[Can't let this slide!]
Let's just really play the Mafia game now.

267
00:08:27,040 --> 00:08:28,876
It wasn't me.

268
00:08:28,876 --> 00:08:30,830
We weren't even in the same room.

269
00:08:30,830 --> 00:08:33,113
[But what if you are the accomplice?]
So if it is you…

270
00:08:33,113 --> 00:08:35,122
- I said I'll go in the water!
- You'll go in?

271
00:08:35,122 --> 00:08:37,918
Was it you?

272
00:08:37,918 --> 00:08:39,732
I'm sorry!

273
00:08:39,732 --> 00:08:41,673
[Caught the accomplice]

274
00:08:41,673 --> 00:08:42,823
Hot sauce!

275
00:08:42,823 --> 00:08:44,291
- Drink the hot sauce!!!
- No wonder!

276
00:08:44,291 --> 00:08:46,293
[The hot sauce pledge was already strange...]
No wonder! This amount is totally doable!

277
00:08:46,293 --> 00:08:48,989
You should've said
you'd pour it all in and drink it!

278
00:08:48,989 --> 00:08:50,464
[They get more annoyed as they think about it]
I had a feeling it was him!

279
00:08:50,464 --> 00:08:52,966
- But he suddenly…!
- Sorry!

280
00:08:52,966 --> 00:08:54,000
- You two ate it?
- Yes.

281
00:08:54,000 --> 00:08:55,802
[A minor commotion among the commoners]
Oh, the two commoners. Okay.

282
00:08:55,802 --> 00:08:58,282
[The pauper is mad]
Then strip the commoners of their titles!

283
00:08:58,282 --> 00:08:59,366
Revoke it!

284
00:08:59,366 --> 00:09:00,718
Should we do it?

285
00:09:00,718 --> 00:09:02,052
This is the prince's authority!

286
00:09:02,052 --> 00:09:03,787
[Defending himself]
We didn't pledge that! We didn't!

287
00:09:03,787 --> 00:09:05,525
[All or nothing!]
All King and All Pauper, just go be a pauper!

288
00:09:05,525 --> 00:09:06,680
Just do it!

289
00:09:06,680 --> 00:09:07,718
Nice!

290
00:09:08,949 --> 00:09:10,115
Let's do it!

291
00:09:10,784 --> 00:09:12,786
But I do actually like
having a room to myself.

292
00:09:12,786 --> 00:09:13,921
Come on!

293
00:09:13,921 --> 00:09:15,357
Shin Dong, I'll stay in the bathroom then!

294
00:09:15,357 --> 00:09:18,058
[Throwing a tantrum]
Make all four of us paupers!

295
00:09:18,058 --> 00:09:19,610
Just two is too lonely!

296
00:09:19,610 --> 00:09:21,206
Four paupers sleeping together
is better than two.

297
00:09:21,206 --> 00:09:22,930
[Makes total sense the more they listen]
- It's so great! - All cozy together.

298
00:09:22,930 --> 00:09:24,058
Exactly!

299
00:09:24,058 --> 00:09:26,511
You got to enjoy all the food.

300
00:09:26,511 --> 00:09:27,895
I'll go empty myself out.

301
00:09:27,895 --> 00:09:28,969
Empty what?

302
00:09:28,969 --> 00:09:31,274
Then we'll wait for the princes' decision.

303
00:09:31,274 --> 00:09:33,674
- The princes' decision is…!
- The princes' decision is…!

304
00:09:33,674 --> 00:09:35,642
- Please show leniency!
- Please!

305
00:09:35,642 --> 00:09:36,976
Oh, why? A final closing argument...?

306
00:09:36,976 --> 00:09:38,998
- I will make the closing argument!
- The closing argument!

307
00:09:38,998 --> 00:09:40,044
Yes.

308
00:09:40,044 --> 00:09:42,142
DAWN was the one who first…

309
00:09:43,183 --> 00:09:44,551
[The enabler]
Wow, this…!

310
00:09:44,551 --> 00:09:45,997
[I beg for leniency]
Wow…!

311
00:09:45,997 --> 00:09:47,421
Please only punish DAWN!

312
00:09:47,421 --> 00:09:50,460
DAWN's never even slept in a tent!

313
00:09:50,460 --> 00:09:52,693
[I don't want to…lose my commoner status]
Should we send DAWN away?

314
00:09:52,693 --> 00:09:54,862
Wow, Ji Sung must be really desperate.

315
00:09:54,862 --> 00:09:56,257
My rebuttal!

316
00:09:56,257 --> 00:09:58,799
I really felt bad for Ji Sung. Really!

317
00:09:59,833 --> 00:10:01,285
You all saw earlier!

318
00:10:01,285 --> 00:10:02,503
[Shivering]
He was shivering.

319
00:10:02,503 --> 00:10:04,337
Yeah, so the ramyeon…

320
00:10:04,337 --> 00:10:06,440
But!!!!!! Do you know what's really important?!

321
00:10:06,440 --> 00:10:08,917
That Bowl Noodle Soup was totally mine!

322
00:10:08,917 --> 00:10:10,410
DAWN, that Bowl Noodle Soup was mine.

323
00:10:10,410 --> 00:10:13,113
- Oh, really?
- It was mine.

324
00:10:13,113 --> 00:10:16,483
Was it DAWN who brought up
eating the Cup Ramyeon?

325
00:10:16,483 --> 00:10:17,878
Wasn't it you?

326
00:10:18,519 --> 00:10:20,020
[The culprits start fighting each other]
Who was it?

327
00:10:20,020 --> 00:10:21,855
Just be honest.

328
00:10:21,855 --> 00:10:25,459
[Only one of the two survives]
Only one of the two…!

329
00:10:25,459 --> 00:10:27,710
We'll only send one of you!

330
00:10:27,710 --> 00:10:29,095
Huh? Was it me?

331
00:10:29,095 --> 00:10:30,096
"Huh, was it me?"

332
00:10:30,096 --> 00:10:32,165
Let's play it back!

333
00:10:32,165 --> 00:10:33,443
Was there no camera?

334
00:10:33,443 --> 00:10:34,360
[VAR]
Okay, you two

335
00:10:34,360 --> 00:10:37,037
[Let's review the video]
Can we get a little help with the ramyeon?

336
00:10:37,037 --> 00:10:40,169
[The culprits were running
the princes' ramyeon errand]

337
00:10:41,044 --> 00:10:43,337
Should we secretly
eat one before we go?

338
00:10:43,337 --> 00:10:45,214
[Fact check 1]
I think no one will notice, right?

339
00:10:45,214 --> 00:10:46,425
[DAWN suggested it first]
If we eat it right away and go?

340
00:10:46,425 --> 00:10:47,634
I looked at Ji Sung,

341
00:10:47,634 --> 00:10:50,053
and he looked way too gaunt.

342
00:10:50,053 --> 00:10:51,179
[This big brother]
As his older brother,

343
00:10:51,179 --> 00:10:52,305
I have to take care of him!

344
00:10:52,305 --> 00:10:53,932
[Gonna eat ramyeon]
Oh, we should eat ramyeon together.

345
00:10:53,932 --> 00:10:55,932
(Definitely not because he wanted to eat it)

346
00:10:56,560 --> 00:11:00,480
[The devil's whisper continues]
Since the noodles take time to cook anyway.

347
00:11:01,261 --> 00:11:03,150
- Should we eat it?
- Wait.

348
00:11:03,150 --> 00:11:05,098
[Fact check 2]
[Ji Sung agreed too]

349
00:11:05,098 --> 00:11:06,466
[Target spotted]
Should we eat the Bowl Noodle Soup?

350
00:11:06,466 --> 00:11:08,071
This Bowl Noodle Soup too…

351
00:11:08,071 --> 00:11:09,497
I feel like no one would notice.

352
00:11:09,497 --> 00:11:12,615
Since the noodles take time to cook,
let's just eat one here!

353
00:11:12,615 --> 00:11:13,884
Let's split one between us.

354
00:11:13,884 --> 00:11:15,809
But shouldn't we cook this one too?

355
00:11:15,809 --> 00:11:16,977
[Yeah, we have to cook it first]
Let's cook it fast!

356
00:11:16,977 --> 00:11:19,529
- We'll pour the hot water in this one first.
- Oh, okay, okay.

357
00:11:20,584 --> 00:11:23,670
[There's no turning back now]

358
00:11:23,670 --> 00:11:25,881
[Ji Sung turns into a meerkat]

359
00:11:27,548 --> 00:11:30,969
(Definitely not because DAWN wanted to eat it)

360
00:11:31,625 --> 00:11:32,960
The water's finally warm.

361
00:11:32,960 --> 00:11:35,432
We have to hurry and eat this first, so…

362
00:11:35,432 --> 00:11:38,184
[No time to wait for the water to boil]
This…

363
00:11:39,310 --> 00:11:43,460
[Starting to justify the crime]
This is all part of the fun.

364
00:11:44,862 --> 00:11:49,821
[Ready to eat just 1 minute after pouring water]

365
00:11:51,273 --> 00:11:53,547
It's a bit undercooked, though...

366
00:11:53,547 --> 00:11:54,815
[Basically raw]
I'm all about that chewy texture.

367
00:11:54,815 --> 00:11:57,008
Me too, I also really love it that way.

368
00:11:57,912 --> 00:12:00,015
[Flinching at the slightest breeze]

369
00:12:00,415 --> 00:12:04,084
[You are watching the ramyeon heist in action]
Let's dig in.

370
00:12:08,715 --> 00:12:10,715
[The magic of instant happiness]

371
00:12:10,715 --> 00:12:12,633
This is insanely good.

372
00:12:15,389 --> 00:12:17,640
[Pure bliss]

373
00:12:18,058 --> 00:12:20,394
[Took a bite, when someone showed up]

374
00:12:20,394 --> 00:12:21,892
Wow, seriously...!

375
00:12:21,892 --> 00:12:22,771
I thought it was Shin Dong.

376
00:12:22,771 --> 00:12:24,731
Oh, Director!

377
00:12:24,731 --> 00:12:27,020
I thought you were Shin Dong!

378
00:12:27,020 --> 00:12:28,147
I thought it was Shin Dong!

379
00:12:28,147 --> 00:12:31,318
[Audio crew appears (to check the mics)]

380
00:12:32,530 --> 00:12:34,825
[Even though they feel uneasy
and their ramyeon is lukewarm]

381
00:12:34,825 --> 00:12:36,676
But isn't this seriously so delicious?

382
00:12:38,077 --> 00:12:41,998
[Happy ramyeon thieves]

383
00:12:43,458 --> 00:12:45,083
But seriously, this place…

384
00:12:48,171 --> 00:12:51,174
[Hehehehehehehe]

385
00:12:52,301 --> 00:12:55,486
It was a bit crunchy,
but eating in secret made it so delicious.

386
00:12:55,909 --> 00:12:58,240
Shin Dong said it earlier, remember?

387
00:12:58,240 --> 00:13:00,547
- Ramyeon tastes the best when you eat it in secret.
- I know, right?

388
00:13:00,547 --> 00:13:02,727
- We're just doing what he said.
- We're just listening to the king.

389
00:13:02,727 --> 00:13:04,103
[Getting more shameless by the minute]
Exactly.

390
00:13:04,896 --> 00:13:08,775
[Casually savoring the broth too]

391
00:13:08,775 --> 00:13:09,989
Hey, the broth is next level.

392
00:13:09,989 --> 00:13:12,319
[Finally coming to his senses]
But, this must be soggy by now.

393
00:13:12,319 --> 00:13:14,698
- I think we should go now.
- Yeah, let's go, let's go.

394
00:13:14,698 --> 00:13:16,797
Let me throw away the broth.

395
00:13:16,797 --> 00:13:18,398
Wanna throw it away in my body instead?

396
00:13:18,398 --> 00:13:19,333
Oh, this, this!

397
00:13:19,333 --> 00:13:21,705
- I'll…
- Oh, you're gonna drink it?

398
00:13:21,705 --> 00:13:23,139
[The best cleanup method is]

399
00:13:23,139 --> 00:13:24,540
[eating it all up!]

400
00:13:24,540 --> 00:13:26,084
But seriously, it's so good.

401
00:13:27,206 --> 00:13:28,641
[Exhibit 1]
We gotta throw away the trash properly.

402
00:13:28,641 --> 00:13:30,243
[Ramyeon trash]
Can we just hide it like this?

403
00:13:30,243 --> 00:13:32,078
[Evidence disposal complete]

404
00:13:32,078 --> 00:13:33,800
Oh, okay. It's over there.

405
00:13:33,800 --> 00:13:35,449
- Check your lips.
- Lemme see, lemme see.

406
00:13:35,449 --> 00:13:37,552
[Exhibit 2]
Wait, you got some on you.

407
00:13:37,552 --> 00:13:39,485
[Ji Sung has ramyeon traces around his mouth]
Hold on.

408
00:13:39,485 --> 00:13:40,787
[Evidence wiped clean]

409
00:13:40,787 --> 00:13:42,623
[Sweet DAWN]

410
00:13:42,623 --> 00:13:44,394
Oh, it's fine, it's fine.

411
00:13:44,394 --> 00:13:45,993
[Even when they all ate ramyeon together]
This is just too good.

412
00:13:45,993 --> 00:13:47,492
This is seriously delicious.

413
00:13:47,492 --> 00:13:48,464
[Giving his best salivating performance]
This is really…

414
00:13:48,464 --> 00:13:50,117
There's not much left.

415
00:13:50,692 --> 00:13:53,069
[and fake act of desperation]
Wow!

416
00:13:53,069 --> 00:13:54,738
What about me?

417
00:13:54,738 --> 00:13:56,654
[Scraping the bottom of the bowl for show]

418
00:13:56,654 --> 00:13:58,764
- You scrape at it even if there's nothing.
- You end up scraping at it.

419
00:13:58,764 --> 00:14:00,240
I barely ate, but I feel full.

420
00:14:00,240 --> 00:14:02,146
- We only had a bite, but we feel full, right?
- Yeah.

421
00:14:02,146 --> 00:14:04,611
[Because we ate earlier]

422
00:14:04,611 --> 00:14:06,046
[Even while talking about the ramyeon]
What else is left over?

423
00:14:06,046 --> 00:14:07,748
[Cup Ramyeon!]
Bowl Noodle Soup.

424
00:14:07,748 --> 00:14:09,043
Bowl Noodle Soup and…

425
00:14:09,043 --> 00:14:10,450
[Eye contact]
If you add perilla powder to Bowl Noodle Soup,

426
00:14:10,450 --> 00:14:12,186
[LOL]
it tastes like pork bone soup.

427
00:14:12,186 --> 00:14:13,813
[Desperately trying to keep a straight face]
- Oh, really? - Yeah.

428
00:14:13,813 --> 00:14:15,289
I ate way too much
Bowl Noodle Soup back in Korea.

429
00:14:15,289 --> 00:14:17,143
[Playing dumb to avoid getting caught]
Thanks for the food.

430
00:14:17,758 --> 00:14:19,526
Then, when you were running our errand?

431
00:14:19,526 --> 00:14:20,894
Yeah!

432
00:14:20,894 --> 00:14:22,640
- We ate it while making your ramyeon.
- Yeah, that's right.

433
00:14:22,640 --> 00:14:25,566
[Finally confessing openly]
Oh, then! That's when you ate it?

434
00:14:25,566 --> 00:14:27,801
We ate it with cold, lukewarm water.

435
00:14:27,801 --> 00:14:29,355
You're unbelievable.

436
00:14:29,355 --> 00:14:30,398
Well, as for me,

437
00:14:30,398 --> 00:14:31,949
[Sweeping the past under the rug]
I don't dwell on the past.

438
00:14:31,949 --> 00:14:33,005
Is that so?

439
00:14:33,005 --> 00:14:34,707
- Your Honor!
- Yes!

440
00:14:34,707 --> 00:14:36,609
- Are you the judge?
- Yes, I'm the judge.

441
00:14:36,609 --> 00:14:38,281
[Court is in session at the dinner table]
- Your Honor. - Yes.

442
00:14:38,281 --> 00:14:40,480
- As the pauper team's counsel…
- Yes.

443
00:14:40,480 --> 00:14:41,785
we ask that DAWN sleeps with us.

444
00:14:41,785 --> 00:14:43,020
[We want DAWN, the culprit!]

445
00:14:43,020 --> 00:14:44,451
What are you talking about?

446
00:14:44,451 --> 00:14:46,787
- That's not even in the rules.
- Alright!

447
00:14:46,787 --> 00:14:49,367
[Rushing to judgment]
What do you mean by "Alright", Shin Dong?

448
00:14:49,367 --> 00:14:50,751
[Already ready to deliver the verdict]
Please don't do that, seriously.

449
00:14:50,751 --> 00:14:51,560
Alright!

450
00:14:51,560 --> 00:14:52,920
- Now that it's come to this…
- Come to this?

451
00:14:52,920 --> 00:14:56,048
we can't just let them off
without any punishment.

452
00:14:56,048 --> 00:14:57,267
Please give them a punishment!

453
00:14:57,267 --> 00:14:58,565
Right, so…

454
00:14:58,565 --> 00:15:01,132
They were upgraded to commoners,

455
00:15:01,132 --> 00:15:02,806
[To undo all that is a bit…]
but taking back the titles feels a bit…

456
00:15:02,806 --> 00:15:04,332
- Absolutely not!
- So!

457
00:15:04,332 --> 00:15:06,206
So! Okay!

458
00:15:06,206 --> 00:15:07,808
We, the princes,

459
00:15:07,808 --> 00:15:10,646
[Prince Court Final Verdict]
have gathered everyone's opinions,

460
00:15:10,646 --> 00:15:12,545
- and sentence DAWN…!
- DAWN!

461
00:15:12,545 --> 00:15:14,882
to 1 hour of pauper life.

462
00:15:14,882 --> 00:15:16,884
[Order]
[The defendant is sentenced to 1 hour as a pauper]

463
00:15:16,884 --> 00:15:18,252
[Objection]

464
00:15:18,252 --> 00:15:19,614
1 hour is too short!

465
00:15:19,614 --> 00:15:22,326
So that he can
at least experience the tent…!

466
00:15:22,326 --> 00:15:23,826
Honorable Judge!

467
00:15:23,826 --> 00:15:25,786
I will not receive any more honor.

468
00:15:25,786 --> 00:15:27,728
- Less-honorable Judge!
- Yes.

469
00:15:27,728 --> 00:15:29,595
I object!!

470
00:15:29,595 --> 00:15:30,831
Is this "The Truman Show" or what? Seriously!

471
00:15:30,831 --> 00:15:32,299
1 hour is just not enough!

472
00:15:32,299 --> 00:15:34,284
What's not enough?
1 hour is plenty!

473
00:15:34,284 --> 00:15:35,769
[An impassioned plea]
1 hour really isn't enough!

474
00:15:35,769 --> 00:15:38,972
In 1 hour, the stock market
can fluctuate several times!

475
00:15:38,972 --> 00:15:42,575
Please, let me
share a tent with DAWN.

476
00:15:42,575 --> 00:15:44,344
This court is adjourned!

477
00:15:44,344 --> 00:15:45,813
[Bang! Bang! Bang!]
No! No!

478
00:15:45,813 --> 00:15:48,182
- This trial is invalid!!!!
- Thank you!

479
00:15:48,182 --> 00:15:49,536
[Thank you for the leniency]
I'll work hard from now on!

480
00:15:49,536 --> 00:15:50,995
- Thank you!
- Oh, come on!

481
00:15:51,605 --> 00:15:54,847
[Deeply invested]
The justice system is rotten!

482
00:15:54,847 --> 00:15:56,776
What came to mind while playing the games…

483
00:15:56,776 --> 00:15:59,279
I should've gone
to make the ramyeon myself...

484
00:15:59,279 --> 00:16:01,282
I should've made the ramyeon...

485
00:16:01,282 --> 00:16:03,366
and eaten 2 cups of ramyeon.

486
00:16:03,366 --> 00:16:05,868
If I'd known I'd end up a pauper
and not get to eat anything,

487
00:16:05,868 --> 00:16:09,036
I should've just gone and eaten
everything I wanted before coming back...

488
00:16:09,036 --> 00:16:11,416
[A day filled with late regrets]
Yeah, I'm regretting it a bit.

489
00:16:11,416 --> 00:16:14,173
This is why I never share
a table with the paupers!

490
00:16:14,173 --> 00:16:15,776
[Table Courtroom]
[Crime and Ramyeon]

491
00:16:15,776 --> 00:16:17,444
[The End]
This is seriously hilarious. Wow.

492
00:16:17,444 --> 00:16:19,463
But where are we even sleeping?

493
00:16:19,463 --> 00:16:24,679
The original place we chose
for the paupers to set up the tent was…

494
00:16:24,679 --> 00:16:26,253
You saw it earlier
while searching for clues.

495
00:16:26,253 --> 00:16:27,332
[During "Conversations with the Ancients"]
You know, that rocky hill?

496
00:16:27,332 --> 00:16:28,850
- No, not there!
- That was the original spot?

497
00:16:28,850 --> 00:16:29,876
That was the original spot.

498
00:16:29,876 --> 00:16:31,352
We'll really get blown away there…

499
00:16:31,352 --> 00:16:33,976
Seeing today's wind,
we thought it wouldn't work out.

500
00:16:33,976 --> 00:16:35,023
We can't, we can't.

501
00:16:35,023 --> 00:16:38,359
So we prepared a place
that's safer and flatter.

502
00:16:38,359 --> 00:16:40,236
- Where? Where's that?
- Where exactly?

503
00:16:40,236 --> 00:16:43,471
The stairs that you came up on.

504
00:16:43,471 --> 00:16:44,357
Wait, hold on.

505
00:16:44,357 --> 00:16:45,742
[The paupers are sleeping on the stairs]
That's way better, way better.

506
00:16:45,742 --> 00:16:46,673
Honorable…

507
00:16:46,673 --> 00:16:49,996
If you look at the stairs going down,
there's one unusually big step.

508
00:16:49,996 --> 00:16:51,914
- Oh, in the middle.
- Oh, there, there!

509
00:16:51,914 --> 00:16:54,041
Honorable Producer!

510
00:16:54,417 --> 00:16:56,950
[The highly respectful type]
I formally object!

511
00:16:56,950 --> 00:16:58,842
The stone part over there

512
00:16:58,842 --> 00:17:00,775
could hurt our bones, right?

513
00:17:00,775 --> 00:17:03,202
We'll lay down a padded mat for you anyway.

514
00:17:03,202 --> 00:17:05,425
- I've been a pauper a few times now, right?
- Yes.

515
00:17:05,425 --> 00:17:06,527
[2-time pauper]
There is a padded mat.

516
00:17:06,527 --> 00:17:07,342
Right.

517
00:17:07,342 --> 00:17:08,723
[1-time pauper]
I know that too!

518
00:17:08,723 --> 00:17:11,213
- You know?
- Honorable Producer!

519
00:17:11,213 --> 00:17:12,432
Our sleeping spot…!

520
00:17:12,432 --> 00:17:14,854
Even ghosts look better
on a full stomach!

521
00:17:14,854 --> 00:17:16,355
[We will sleep at the restaurant]
We will sleep right here.

522
00:17:16,355 --> 00:17:18,074
Lee Teuk, this place is even windier!

523
00:17:18,074 --> 00:17:21,475
No, because there's a partition down here.

524
00:17:21,475 --> 00:17:23,877
Lee Teuk, I'm sitting right next to it, right?

525
00:17:23,877 --> 00:17:25,573
It's super windy right here!

526
00:17:25,573 --> 00:17:27,350
[But it's blowing sand down there…]
I think it'd be better here, because..

527
00:17:27,350 --> 00:17:29,249
- The wind's blowing so much sand over there.
- Exactly!

528
00:17:29,249 --> 00:17:31,518
[On point]
- But you're pitching tents. - That's true...

529
00:17:31,518 --> 00:17:34,787
When we decide on a place,
we have one rule we try to stick to.

530
00:17:34,787 --> 00:17:38,158
[Paupers' accommodation rule]
- What kind of rule? - No roofs allowed.

531
00:17:38,158 --> 00:17:39,726
The stars are our blankets!

532
00:17:39,726 --> 00:17:42,894
Can't we do a little location scouting first?

533
00:17:42,894 --> 00:17:44,882
[Princes' mercy]
We'll allow some location scouting.

534
00:17:44,882 --> 00:17:46,400
Just make sure to follow that one rule.

535
00:17:46,400 --> 00:17:47,945
[Paupers' accommodation rule 1]
Right, you can't have a roof.

536
00:17:47,945 --> 00:17:49,436
- No roofs?
- Yes.

537
00:17:49,436 --> 00:17:51,432
[Paupers' accommodation rule 2]
You can't sleep somewhere higher than the princes.

538
00:17:51,432 --> 00:17:53,173
[Royal approval]

539
00:17:53,173 --> 00:17:54,708
Didn't you just make up the second rule?

540
00:17:54,708 --> 00:17:56,210
[Correct!]

541
00:17:56,210 --> 00:17:57,881
[The princes will head to their comfy quarters]
Alright, the princes will go now.

542
00:17:57,881 --> 00:17:58,979
Where are you going?

543
00:17:58,979 --> 00:18:00,480
We're going to our rooms.

544
00:18:00,480 --> 00:18:01,815
See you in an hour, DAWN.

545
00:18:01,815 --> 00:18:03,553
Okay!

546
00:18:03,553 --> 00:18:05,452
- Let's go!
- Yeah, let's go!

547
00:18:05,452 --> 00:18:07,643
Did you sell me out because
you were scared of becoming a pauper?

548
00:18:07,643 --> 00:18:09,017
[Sorry]

549
00:18:09,017 --> 00:18:11,477
[Biggest beneficiary]
Thank goodness, it's just probation!

550
00:18:11,992 --> 00:18:14,184
Oh, it's cold!

551
00:18:15,732 --> 00:18:18,960
[As if it were planned, the paupers remain]

552
00:18:18,960 --> 00:18:21,445
[Munch, munch...]

553
00:18:23,103 --> 00:18:24,908
This is seriously delicious.

554
00:18:24,908 --> 00:18:27,841
[Fries forever]

555
00:18:27,841 --> 00:18:29,693
Wow, they left all of this?!

556
00:18:30,244 --> 00:18:32,179
Those pauper-like fools!

557
00:18:32,179 --> 00:18:33,705
[Glare]

558
00:18:34,208 --> 00:18:36,250
[Pauper to pauper]
Those pauper-like fools! Leaving food behind!

559
00:18:36,250 --> 00:18:37,751
[Scolding]
You will pay for this!

560
00:18:37,751 --> 00:18:39,619
You'll be forced to eat
all of this in the afterlife!

561
00:18:39,619 --> 00:18:43,134
[Classic boomer energy]
Kids these days have no drive! No grit!

562
00:18:43,134 --> 00:18:45,809
They don't even know
what tear-soaked bread tastes like.

563
00:18:46,927 --> 00:18:49,229
Excuse me.

564
00:18:49,229 --> 00:18:51,364
Microwave, heat up!

565
00:18:51,364 --> 00:18:52,993
[Rich accent]
Please heat it up!

566
00:18:54,968 --> 00:18:56,387
Ugh… So cold…

567
00:18:57,649 --> 00:18:59,041
Ugh, seriously!!

568
00:19:00,193 --> 00:19:02,306
This is going too far!

569
00:19:02,306 --> 00:19:05,738
[Yo Han, stuff your face first]

570
00:19:05,738 --> 00:19:07,634
(Trembling)

571
00:19:08,782 --> 00:19:11,110
[Calm again]
But this is really good.

572
00:19:12,386 --> 00:19:14,112
[Eating every last crumb]

573
00:19:14,749 --> 00:19:15,959
Yo Han, make sure to grab the water.

574
00:19:15,959 --> 00:19:17,313
Oh, the water!

575
00:19:21,089 --> 00:19:23,675
Lee Teuk, other than Day 1,
this is your first time as a pauper, right?

576
00:19:23,675 --> 00:19:25,218
[Lol...]

577
00:19:25,218 --> 00:19:26,428
It's all about how you
start and finish,

578
00:19:26,428 --> 00:19:27,804
but both my start and finish
were a total disaster.

579
00:19:27,804 --> 00:19:29,514
Oh, right! That's true, Lee Teuk.

580
00:19:30,390 --> 00:19:32,642
- Let's go.
- Lee Teuk, let's go check out the site!

581
00:19:32,642 --> 00:19:34,314
Let's go.

582
00:19:35,494 --> 00:19:36,643
(Commoner's bed) (Prince's bed)
I'm wondering…

583
00:19:36,643 --> 00:19:38,011
[Johnny & Ji Sung]
[Chilling together]

584
00:19:38,011 --> 00:19:40,080
Should we sleep with this open or closed?

585
00:19:40,080 --> 00:19:41,167
[Leave it open]
Totally…!

586
00:19:41,167 --> 00:19:43,449
I'm gonna catch the sunrise.

587
00:19:43,449 --> 00:19:44,822
- You're gonna watch the sunrise…?
- Yeah.

588
00:19:44,822 --> 00:19:45,853
Why?

589
00:19:45,853 --> 00:19:48,622
I'm curious, you know,
being on an island like this...

590
00:19:48,622 --> 00:19:50,485
[First day as a commoner]
What time's the sunrise?

591
00:19:50,485 --> 00:19:52,138
[Comfort brings out his romantic side]
Around 5 or 6 am.

592
00:19:52,559 --> 00:19:53,789
Let me check…

593
00:19:53,789 --> 00:19:55,557
Egypt...

594
00:19:55,557 --> 00:19:56,624
[Heh...]

595
00:19:56,624 --> 00:19:57,764
Heh, like...

596
00:19:57,764 --> 00:20:00,601
[So obvious]
"Egypt sunrise time."

597
00:20:00,601 --> 00:20:03,170
[Correct]

598
00:20:03,170 --> 00:20:05,533
[On the same wavelength]
I just got goosebumps.

599
00:20:06,173 --> 00:20:08,961
[If you wanna see the sunrise,
better sleep quickly]

600
00:20:09,436 --> 00:20:11,678
- Wanna do a face pack?
- Nah!

601
00:20:11,678 --> 00:20:13,647
I'm good.

602
00:20:13,647 --> 00:20:15,632
[Self-care king]
I'm gonna do it!

603
00:20:16,227 --> 00:20:18,970
[Finally lying down on
my small, precious bed]

604
00:20:21,655 --> 00:20:23,257
You're tired, huh?

605
00:20:23,257 --> 00:20:25,972
Yeah, tired but feeling great.

606
00:20:26,460 --> 00:20:29,229
I can't believe I'm not in a tent…!

607
00:20:30,130 --> 00:20:32,907
[Even though his tentmates kept rotating out,]

608
00:20:33,534 --> 00:20:35,121
[Ji Sung was always present in the tent…]

609
00:20:35,121 --> 00:20:36,681
(Resident ghost)

610
00:20:37,604 --> 00:20:39,489
[Johnny leaves to shower first]
I'll go wash up.

611
00:20:39,489 --> 00:20:40,741
Okay.

612
00:20:41,544 --> 00:20:44,878
[Yaaaaaawn]

613
00:20:44,878 --> 00:20:48,382
[Oh, right]
I need to check the sunrise time.

614
00:20:49,917 --> 00:20:52,120
(Egypt... sunrise... time...)

615
00:20:52,120 --> 00:20:55,441
[Current time 11:42 pm]
Wow, 5:13 is way too brutal.

616
00:20:56,223 --> 00:20:59,078
Then I'll...

617
00:20:59,078 --> 00:21:01,189
Since the sunrise is at 5:13...

618
00:21:01,189 --> 00:21:02,862
I'll wake up around 5.

619
00:21:03,997 --> 00:21:05,485
[Hmm...]

620
00:21:05,485 --> 00:21:07,695
[Not feeling confident]

621
00:21:09,069 --> 00:21:11,173
[Let's just lie down first]

622
00:21:11,173 --> 00:21:12,780
[Plops!]

623
00:21:16,013 --> 00:21:19,181
What I'm seeing over there
can't be a mosquito, right…?

624
00:21:19,880 --> 00:21:23,033
[The biggest crisis for the bug hater]

625
00:21:24,003 --> 00:21:26,272
[Oh my goodness…]

626
00:21:26,839 --> 00:21:28,287
Whoa! Head rush…

627
00:21:28,287 --> 00:21:29,857
Orthostatic hypotension...

628
00:21:32,679 --> 00:21:35,515
(I need to check
what kind of bug that is…)

629
00:21:36,949 --> 00:21:39,118
[It's definitely a bug...]
I'm pretty sure…

630
00:21:39,118 --> 00:21:40,436
(Glance)

631
00:21:41,120 --> 00:21:43,814
[Failed to keep a brave front]

632
00:21:45,500 --> 00:21:48,153
(Ha... if it falls on the bed…)

633
00:21:49,946 --> 00:21:53,883
[Uh-oh]

634
00:21:55,760 --> 00:21:57,787
[Giving up]
Let's just sleep...

635
00:21:58,622 --> 00:22:02,308
[While Ji Sung's spiraling over the bug]

636
00:22:03,810 --> 00:22:06,582
But instead of going there,
why not go over here on the sand…

637
00:22:06,582 --> 00:22:08,130
[The criminal and paupers inspect the site]
Because the tent needs to stay up.

638
00:22:09,649 --> 00:22:11,030
[Location conditions]
Where should we really sleep?

639
00:22:11,030 --> 00:22:12,844
[No roof allowed]
[Lower than the princes' accommodation]

640
00:22:12,844 --> 00:22:14,388
Lee Teuk, you choose!

641
00:22:15,202 --> 00:22:16,743
[Hard rock floor]
Do you prefer firm beds?

642
00:22:16,743 --> 00:22:18,958
[vs Soft sandy floor]
Or do you like soft beds?

643
00:22:21,608 --> 00:22:24,213
Since you have the most
pauper experience here...

644
00:22:24,912 --> 00:22:26,880
[Pauper: 2 / Pauper: 0 / Pauper: 3]
I was basically an ALL-Pauper.

645
00:22:26,880 --> 00:22:28,791
- Yeah, since you have the most experience…
- Yes.

646
00:22:28,791 --> 00:22:31,151
You tell me where it's better to sleep.

647
00:22:31,151 --> 00:22:33,187
[Yo Han's pick: hard rock floor]
I definitely think it's better to sleep here,

648
00:22:33,187 --> 00:22:35,722
because, we've got mats, right?

649
00:22:35,722 --> 00:22:37,324
[Basic option: 2 toppers]
Lay down 2 of them.

650
00:22:37,324 --> 00:22:38,567
[Extra option: 1 sleeping bag per person]
And then we add sleeping bags.

651
00:22:38,567 --> 00:22:40,316
- Okay.
- So,

652
00:22:40,316 --> 00:22:42,062
[Current pauper leader makes the call]
the floor may be hard, but it's flat.

653
00:22:42,062 --> 00:22:43,530
- Yeah, that's right.
- Yes.

654
00:22:43,530 --> 00:22:46,594
[I'm counting on you, Yo Han]
Let's set it out here.

655
00:22:47,266 --> 00:22:48,546
[Setting up the tent in the strong winds]

656
00:22:48,546 --> 00:22:50,272
Are we setting it up now?

657
00:22:50,938 --> 00:22:53,926
But DAWN's never set up a tent before.

658
00:22:53,926 --> 00:22:55,876
This is totally…

659
00:22:55,876 --> 00:22:57,077
[3-time prince DAWN is new to the tent]
It's my first time doing this.

660
00:22:57,077 --> 00:22:59,160
This might blow away, so be careful.

661
00:22:59,618 --> 00:23:00,434
This…

662
00:23:00,434 --> 00:23:03,186
[The veteran paupers show how it's done]
Like this, then like that.

663
00:23:03,828 --> 00:23:05,188
You have to line up the joints right.

664
00:23:05,188 --> 00:23:08,121
- It's the other way around. This goes on top.
- Redo it, redo it.

665
00:23:08,121 --> 00:23:10,958
[Wiiiiiind]
Oh, it's turning around!

666
00:23:10,958 --> 00:23:12,191
We have to hold it down!

667
00:23:12,191 --> 00:23:14,416
We have to hold it down…

668
00:23:15,295 --> 00:23:17,329
We have to hold it down…

669
00:23:17,329 --> 00:23:19,099
[Heavy supplies incoming]
And the mat goes in!

670
00:23:19,099 --> 00:23:20,711
[A quick emergency fix]

671
00:23:21,133 --> 00:23:25,038
[Our home can't fly away…!]
Sleeping bag, sleeping bag!

672
00:23:25,672 --> 00:23:27,841
(Struggling)
Put these on both sides like this.

673
00:23:27,841 --> 00:23:28,976
Like this.

674
00:23:28,976 --> 00:23:30,836
(Hmm...)

675
00:23:30,836 --> 00:23:33,447
[Quickly bailing]
I think it's been an hour already.

676
00:23:33,447 --> 00:23:34,648
[Disappointed]
DAWN, it's only been 2 minutes.

677
00:23:34,648 --> 00:23:35,949
Oh, really?

678
00:23:35,949 --> 00:23:38,519
Come on in!
Welcome to our humble home!

679
00:23:38,519 --> 00:23:40,986
[A not-so-exciting invitation]
Let's have a fun time.

680
00:23:40,986 --> 00:23:42,057
[Actual floor space]
Wow, it's pretty spacious.

681
00:23:42,057 --> 00:23:44,593
- Yeah, come on in.
- Three people can sleep here comfortably.

682
00:23:44,593 --> 00:23:47,102
But when you come in,
please make sure to organize your shoes.

683
00:23:47,102 --> 00:23:48,131
[Grumpy]
Yeah.

684
00:23:48,131 --> 00:23:49,498
[I'm not planning to sleep here…]
I'll be heading out soon anyways…

685
00:23:49,498 --> 00:23:52,232
(Neatly placed)
No, you should sleep over!

686
00:23:52,232 --> 00:23:54,468
[Coming in is up to you,]
You're free to come in whenever you want,

687
00:23:54,468 --> 00:23:55,469
[but leaving is up to me]
but when it comes to leaving…

688
00:23:55,469 --> 00:23:56,823
- Oh, really?
- Yeah.

689
00:23:56,823 --> 00:23:59,342
[Regret]
I shouldn't have eaten that ramyeon…

690
00:24:00,105 --> 00:24:01,842
[Quickly settling in]
But now that I'm here,

691
00:24:01,842 --> 00:24:03,954
- it's a bit less cold…
- Right?

692
00:24:03,954 --> 00:24:04,496
You can even see the moon.

693
00:24:04,496 --> 00:24:05,979
[Blocked]

694
00:24:05,979 --> 00:24:06,999
You can even see the stars...

695
00:24:06,999 --> 00:24:08,582
[Blocked]

696
00:24:08,582 --> 00:24:12,697
[It's still kinda romantic...?]
The view's nice. It's quite romantic, Lee Teuk.

697
00:24:16,067 --> 00:24:18,527
[Commoner DAWN, completely zoning out]

698
00:24:18,945 --> 00:24:23,350
[and the paupers,
feeling hopeless about their future]

699
00:24:24,642 --> 00:24:27,066
(Let's try it this way)

700
00:24:27,066 --> 00:24:28,146
[Leg stretch]

701
00:24:28,146 --> 00:24:29,022
[Trying anything to survive]
Like this?

702
00:24:29,022 --> 00:24:30,315
- Sleep like this.
- Like this, like this.

703
00:24:30,315 --> 00:24:32,639
- Sleep like this.
- With this kind of vibe.

704
00:24:32,639 --> 00:24:34,474
[Chills]
Wow, but this is dangerous...

705
00:24:34,474 --> 00:24:36,992
There's a cactus right in front of us.

706
00:24:38,212 --> 00:24:40,225
[Dangerous]
If it falls, it'll land right on us.

707
00:24:40,225 --> 00:24:42,170
I don't think I can sleep.

708
00:24:42,683 --> 00:24:44,651
Yo Han! Is today the hardest day
in your pauper life?

709
00:24:44,651 --> 00:24:46,799
- Yeah, today's definitely the hardest...
- Oh, really?

710
00:24:46,799 --> 00:24:48,686
Were you a pauper
on the second day too?

711
00:24:48,686 --> 00:24:50,435
I've been a pauper
straight since the second day.

712
00:24:50,435 --> 00:24:52,170
- Oh, non-stop?
- Yeah.

713
00:24:52,793 --> 00:24:54,712
[Pauper accommodation #2 was just romantic]
Honestly, the first time on the rooftop

714
00:24:54,712 --> 00:24:56,530
was quite romantic.

715
00:24:56,530 --> 00:24:58,163
The second one was
right in front of the cruise.

716
00:24:58,163 --> 00:24:59,510
[Pauper accommodation #3 with a Nile River view]
That spot was pretty nice, too.

717
00:24:59,510 --> 00:25:02,336
It was a bit lonely,
but it still felt like we were part of the cruise.

718
00:25:02,336 --> 00:25:04,203
But that night

719
00:25:04,203 --> 00:25:06,406
was the absolute worst of the worst.

720
00:25:06,406 --> 00:25:09,943
This might not show well on camera,

721
00:25:09,943 --> 00:25:13,126
but the wind was so strong
that when you sat or stood up,

722
00:25:13,126 --> 00:25:14,747
it pushed your body back.

723
00:25:14,747 --> 00:25:17,351
That island is literally an island of the wind.

724
00:25:17,351 --> 00:25:20,656
I thought Lee Teuk and Yo Han
couldn't possibly sleep there.

725
00:25:20,656 --> 00:25:22,401
But honestly,

726
00:25:22,401 --> 00:25:25,940
it didn't really matter.
I just wanted to leave as soon as possible.

727
00:25:25,940 --> 00:25:27,461
Should we try blocking it with this?

728
00:25:27,461 --> 00:25:29,767
[Let's just try anything]
Wait, I think we need to fix this a bit.

729
00:25:30,430 --> 00:25:32,668
[Zipping up the window to survive]

730
00:25:32,668 --> 00:25:34,052
Is it good now?

731
00:25:34,868 --> 00:25:36,770
[A ray of hope!]
Oh, it's not flying off...?

732
00:25:36,770 --> 00:25:38,049
We can totally sleep in this!

733
00:25:38,049 --> 00:25:39,573
It got way better.

734
00:25:39,573 --> 00:25:42,011
This tent is really sturdy!

735
00:25:42,011 --> 00:25:43,763
[Running away]
Oh, wait!

736
00:25:43,763 --> 00:25:45,640
Hey! Hey!

737
00:25:45,640 --> 00:25:46,558
Hey…

738
00:25:46,558 --> 00:25:48,017
[Stepped out for a second, and the tent's flying]
Hey! Wait!

739
00:25:48,017 --> 00:25:49,518
- Oh, wait!
- Wait, wait, wait, wait!

740
00:25:49,518 --> 00:25:50,645
No, no!

741
00:25:50,645 --> 00:25:51,938
[Wide open]

742
00:25:51,938 --> 00:25:52,920
No, Lee Teuk…

743
00:25:52,920 --> 00:25:54,932
[Snap]
Uh, wait a sec!

744
00:25:54,932 --> 00:25:56,234
- Agh, Lee Teuk!!!
- Uh, wait a sec!

745
00:25:56,234 --> 00:25:57,790
- Oh, our house!!!!!!
- Uh, wait a sec!

746
00:25:57,790 --> 00:25:59,528
[On the verge of losing their shelter]
Put it down… Doesn't it move this way? Right?

747
00:25:59,528 --> 00:26:00,694
(Glance)
It's this.

748
00:26:00,694 --> 00:26:02,198
Look over there.

749
00:26:02,198 --> 00:26:04,157
Look at the prince's accommodation over there.

750
00:26:04,157 --> 00:26:06,233
You okay there?

751
00:26:06,233 --> 00:26:08,368
Please let us sleep there
for just one night!

752
00:26:08,368 --> 00:26:09,744
[Can't hear]

753
00:26:13,106 --> 00:26:14,975
[No guarantees]
Will we be okay tomorrow?

754
00:26:14,975 --> 00:26:16,777
Wow, this is seriously the worst it's ever been.

755
00:26:16,777 --> 00:26:18,552
Let's just go inside for now.

756
00:26:19,799 --> 00:26:21,842
[Re-entering as the wind dies down]

757
00:26:21,842 --> 00:26:23,980
Ugh, I don't even know anymore.

758
00:26:25,786 --> 00:26:27,955
[The remaining cups of ramyeon
make an appearance]

759
00:26:27,955 --> 00:26:29,556
Here you go.

760
00:26:29,556 --> 00:26:31,249
We'll eat now, Your Highness!

761
00:26:31,249 --> 00:26:32,292
[We'll eat now, Commoner]
Me too.

762
00:26:32,292 --> 00:26:33,493
I'm a pauper for an hour, too.

763
00:26:33,493 --> 00:26:35,829
(Instant block)
Hey, stay back! What are you doing?

764
00:26:35,829 --> 00:26:37,264
You already ate, DAWN.

765
00:26:37,264 --> 00:26:38,365
[Extremely territorial paupers]
What's up with you?

766
00:26:38,365 --> 00:26:41,101
After I ate earlier,
I didn't see this one!

767
00:26:41,101 --> 00:26:43,604
Hey, what are you doing
in a pauper's tent right now?

768
00:26:43,604 --> 00:26:45,460
Is this how you treat your guests?

769
00:26:45,460 --> 00:26:47,002
You must maintain
your dignity, Your Highness!

770
00:26:47,002 --> 00:26:48,411
[You must maintain
your dignity, Commoner]

771
00:26:48,411 --> 00:26:50,511
[Only at times like this...]
Come on, now!

772
00:26:50,511 --> 00:26:53,113
(Taking care of his little pauper brother first)
Here, take a pair of chopsticks.

773
00:26:53,113 --> 00:26:56,317
I've got a favor. If you help me out,
I'll give you the chopsticks.

774
00:26:56,317 --> 00:26:57,337
[A pauper's secret plea to the commoner]
Oh, what is it?

775
00:26:57,337 --> 00:26:58,104
Right now, we…

776
00:26:58,104 --> 00:27:00,687
[Ready to receive]
As you can see,

777
00:27:00,687 --> 00:27:02,823
- if we sleep here and wake up tomorrow...
- Yeah?

778
00:27:02,823 --> 00:27:05,792
One of us is definitely not gonna be here.

779
00:27:05,792 --> 00:27:08,639
I saw that both of
the princes' rooms have terraces.

780
00:27:08,639 --> 00:27:10,129
(Here)
Oh, there's a terrace.

781
00:27:10,129 --> 00:27:11,797
[We can't sleep here]
So that we can pitch our tents on the terrace,

782
00:27:11,797 --> 00:27:13,937
[Help us get permission]
please go up there with me to tell them.

783
00:27:13,937 --> 00:27:15,169
Help us, okay?

784
00:27:15,169 --> 00:27:17,160
- You want me to tell them
- Yeah.

785
00:27:17,160 --> 00:27:18,837
about these miserable conditions, right?

786
00:27:18,837 --> 00:27:21,312
[If you do, you can have first dibs on the ramyeon]
If you tell them, we'll let you have first dibs

787
00:27:21,312 --> 00:27:23,443
on whatever you want to eat.

788
00:27:23,443 --> 00:27:24,930
[Deal]
- Got it! - Oh, seriously?

789
00:27:24,930 --> 00:27:26,547
[Agreement reached]
I did witness your miserable conditions.

790
00:27:26,547 --> 00:27:27,700
Nice, okay.

791
00:27:28,148 --> 00:27:30,059
[The ramyeon is finally ready]
I'll eat it first.

792
00:27:30,928 --> 00:27:33,956
[Slurping up the perfectly cooked noodles]

793
00:27:34,598 --> 00:27:37,658
[And topping it off
with some stir-fried Kimchi]

794
00:27:37,658 --> 00:27:38,893
Wow!

795
00:27:39,726 --> 00:27:42,787
[Chief negotiator DAWN takes a bite too]

796
00:27:43,897 --> 00:27:46,259
[Fiery]
I wanted something spicy so badly!

797
00:27:47,267 --> 00:27:48,889
DAWN, are you gonna eat Kimchi?

798
00:27:48,889 --> 00:27:50,636
No, I'm not.

799
00:27:50,636 --> 00:27:51,515
Then...

800
00:27:51,515 --> 00:27:53,826
[Kimchi added]
I'm gonna put it in!

801
00:27:53,826 --> 00:27:54,660
Kimchigetti!

802
00:27:54,660 --> 00:27:57,771
(Inhaling the food)

803
00:27:59,580 --> 00:28:01,171
Wow…!

804
00:28:02,182 --> 00:28:03,843
[Touched]
Wow, this is seriously delicious...

805
00:28:04,487 --> 00:28:07,988
(Eating well despite the awkward posture)

806
00:28:07,988 --> 00:28:10,032
I wanna mix rice with this.

807
00:28:11,034 --> 00:28:13,261
[In the midst of unimaginably strong winds,]

808
00:28:13,913 --> 00:28:17,625
[the paupers scarf down the food…]

809
00:28:17,625 --> 00:28:19,752
[along with the commoner]

810
00:28:23,297 --> 00:28:25,031
[The Kimchi ends up inside a shoe]

811
00:28:25,031 --> 00:28:25,966
Wait, the shoe…!

812
00:28:25,966 --> 00:28:27,474
[Shocked]
Oh, jeez…

813
00:28:27,474 --> 00:28:29,542
A lot of Kimchi went in there…!

814
00:28:32,473 --> 00:28:33,474
[The chaos never stops at the pauper's house]

815
00:28:33,474 --> 00:28:36,144
There's way more Kimchi juice
in here than I thought!

816
00:28:36,950 --> 00:28:38,819
Tomorrow, my feet are gonna smell…

817
00:28:38,819 --> 00:28:40,801
They're gonna smell like Kimchi!

818
00:28:40,801 --> 00:28:42,200
If you're like, "It smells like Kimchi,"

819
00:28:42,200 --> 00:28:43,567
- just know that it's me.
- Got it, got it.

820
00:28:43,567 --> 00:28:44,971
You know what I mean?

821
00:28:44,971 --> 00:28:46,793
- After living like this one time…
- Yes?

822
00:28:46,793 --> 00:28:47,928
[DAWN experienced
the pauper life for the first time]

823
00:28:47,928 --> 00:28:49,461
- It's kind of…
- Fun?

824
00:28:49,461 --> 00:28:50,797
There's a sense of camaraderie.

825
00:28:50,797 --> 00:28:52,531
So I'll go up there
and quickly pitch the idea to them.

826
00:28:52,531 --> 00:28:53,599
[He wants to get out of here quickly]

827
00:28:53,599 --> 00:28:55,861
[It was a great deal]
Okay, great!

828
00:28:55,861 --> 00:28:58,841
[Quickly escaping the strong winds]
Alright, let's go.

829
00:28:59,773 --> 00:29:02,342
[And heading out to beg the princes]
I'll hold the back.

830
00:29:02,342 --> 00:29:03,410
Let's go!

831
00:29:03,410 --> 00:29:04,766
Just go!

832
00:29:06,026 --> 00:29:07,748
[Wiiiiiiind]
Whoa, whoa, whoa!

833
00:29:07,748 --> 00:29:09,750
[My house is falling apart]
It's falling apart, it's falling apart!

834
00:29:09,750 --> 00:29:11,583
[My precious home...]
Whoa!

835
00:29:11,583 --> 00:29:12,615
I think we need to fold it here.

836
00:29:12,615 --> 00:29:14,390
[They have to fold the tent first
before they do anything else]

837
00:29:14,390 --> 00:29:16,474
I'm holding onto it.

838
00:29:16,474 --> 00:29:17,942
How did you take that off?

839
00:29:18,697 --> 00:29:19,726
That thing…

840
00:29:19,726 --> 00:29:21,461
You have to press this here.

841
00:29:21,461 --> 00:29:23,897
Oh, watch your hand!
Watch your hand!

842
00:29:23,897 --> 00:29:24,965
[Snap]

843
00:29:24,965 --> 00:29:26,592
Huh…?

844
00:29:27,000 --> 00:29:28,886
It's not broken, right...?

845
00:29:28,886 --> 00:29:32,222
[It is broken]
Oh! It's broken!

846
00:29:32,771 --> 00:29:34,368
(Why is he like this…)
- Lee Teuk! - Nah, but this…

847
00:29:34,368 --> 00:29:35,093
It can still stand!

848
00:29:35,093 --> 00:29:36,120
[With the main pole snapping apart]
It can still stand.

849
00:29:36,120 --> 00:29:37,888
- Are you sure?
- Yeah.

850
00:29:37,888 --> 00:29:39,373
[They lose their only shelter]
Why did this break?

851
00:29:39,373 --> 00:29:42,559
The tent got damaged there, and…

852
00:29:42,559 --> 00:29:43,517
Ssp…

853
00:29:43,517 --> 00:29:45,619
It turned into an unavoidable situation...

854
00:29:45,619 --> 00:29:47,287
[We gotta go beg!]
So we went to beg again.

855
00:29:47,287 --> 00:29:49,900
Paupers aren't paupers for nothing.

856
00:29:49,900 --> 00:29:50,802
[The petition begins]
Your High…

857
00:29:50,802 --> 00:29:52,027
Your Highness…!

858
00:29:52,636 --> 00:29:58,398
Your Highness!

859
00:29:58,398 --> 00:30:00,540
[Prince Shin Dong gets up
at the commotion outside the palace]

860
00:30:01,235 --> 00:30:03,189
(What's all this noise?)

861
00:30:03,189 --> 00:30:04,605
We need help!

862
00:30:04,605 --> 00:30:06,108
[Help us, Prince]
The wind's blowing so hard…

863
00:30:06,108 --> 00:30:07,776
The tent broke!

864
00:30:08,475 --> 00:30:10,988
[The wind drowns out the paupers' voices]

865
00:30:10,988 --> 00:30:12,714
I can't hear a word you're saying!

866
00:30:13,173 --> 00:30:14,515
Come on up!

867
00:30:14,515 --> 00:30:16,786
[We're on our way to beg…!]
We're on our way!

868
00:30:16,786 --> 00:30:18,218
Oh, okay!

869
00:30:18,218 --> 00:30:19,543
We got it, we got it.

870
00:30:19,985 --> 00:30:21,088
[Heading up to meet the prince]
Shall we go?

871
00:30:21,088 --> 00:30:22,465
Let's go, let's go!

872
00:30:22,856 --> 00:30:24,976
[Following Commoner DAWN]
Everyone, follow me.

873
00:30:26,072 --> 00:30:28,307
[are the two homeless paupers]

874
00:30:29,857 --> 00:30:33,319
[On the way to appeal to Prince Shin Dong]

875
00:30:34,928 --> 00:30:37,070
- Your Highness!
- Come on in.

876
00:30:37,070 --> 00:30:38,932
[Escaping the wind and entering the palace]
Quickly come in! Quickly!

877
00:30:38,932 --> 00:30:40,973
- Your Highness.
- Quickly come in.

878
00:30:40,973 --> 00:30:43,844
Your Highness,
your citizens have requested to meet you.

879
00:30:43,844 --> 00:30:45,112
What on earth happened?

880
00:30:45,112 --> 00:30:46,580
It was brutal.

881
00:30:46,580 --> 00:30:48,025
[The citizens who survived catastrophic winds]
The wind was blowing so hard.

882
00:30:48,025 --> 00:30:50,444
- It's scary even just being in here.
- Right?

883
00:30:50,444 --> 00:30:51,483
The wind is no joke.

884
00:30:51,483 --> 00:30:53,117
Shin Dong, are you not wearing anything?

885
00:30:53,117 --> 00:30:54,922
[Don't misunderstand]
- No, I am. - Oh, you were.

886
00:30:54,922 --> 00:30:57,031
- Oh, they're pajamas?
- They're my royal pajamas.

887
00:30:57,031 --> 00:30:59,487
- I thought it was just your bare skin.
- Oh, really?

888
00:30:59,487 --> 00:31:00,382
So, what do you want me to do about it?

889
00:31:00,382 --> 00:31:02,171
[Prince Shin Dong, please hear us out]
Go ahead and tell me.

890
00:31:02,171 --> 00:31:04,164
I think we need to explain the entire story.

891
00:31:04,164 --> 00:31:06,398
We asked the Commoner for a favor.

892
00:31:06,398 --> 00:31:07,644
[Because the whole house flew away]
Since it was blowing away…

893
00:31:07,644 --> 00:31:09,169
Since the tent was blowing away,

894
00:31:09,169 --> 00:31:12,288
[Trying to move to the prince's terrace]
we wanted to ask to set it up here.

895
00:31:12,288 --> 00:31:15,307
[It was when they were carrying the tent up here]
So, we were carrying the tent up…

896
00:31:15,806 --> 00:31:17,542
We were carrying
the whole thing in one piece.

897
00:31:17,542 --> 00:31:18,686
[The winds got even stronger]
But over there,

898
00:31:18,686 --> 00:31:20,416
the winds got stronger the higher we climbed up.

899
00:31:20,416 --> 00:31:21,851
You should've folded
the tent before bringing it up!

900
00:31:21,851 --> 00:31:23,283
And so!

901
00:31:23,283 --> 00:31:25,077
- We were gonna fold it here.
- We were gonna fold it.

902
00:31:25,077 --> 00:31:26,856
- While folding it…
- Did it break?

903
00:31:26,856 --> 00:31:29,625
We were folding it, but the wind
pressed down on it, and it snapped.

904
00:31:30,151 --> 00:31:33,291
[They really became paupers
with nowhere to sleep]

905
00:31:33,291 --> 00:31:34,263
(So what?)
What do you want me to do about it?

906
00:31:34,263 --> 00:31:35,929
What do you mean?

907
00:31:35,929 --> 00:31:38,365
Could you maybe let us
sleep in your bedroom tonight?

908
00:31:38,365 --> 00:31:40,447
[Sneaking in their main request]
I'd love to, but there's no room here.

909
00:31:40,447 --> 00:31:42,955
[Please let us sleep
anywhere in the prince's room…]

910
00:31:42,955 --> 00:31:44,456
Can we come here and sleep?

911
00:31:44,456 --> 00:31:45,498
Of course!

912
00:31:45,498 --> 00:31:46,725
[Just sleep anywhere]
If there's a place, just sleep wherever.

913
00:31:46,725 --> 00:31:47,559
[Compassion]
Just anywhere?

914
00:31:47,559 --> 00:31:48,809
Sure! But, wait,

915
00:31:48,809 --> 00:31:51,078
you have to pay for the tent.

916
00:31:51,078 --> 00:31:52,988
[Quickly throwing him under the bus]
Lee Teuk broke it.

917
00:31:52,988 --> 00:31:54,648
I broke it?

918
00:31:54,648 --> 00:31:56,650
[Tends to set the record straight]
Was it me? I broke it?

919
00:31:56,650 --> 00:31:58,852
Okay, okay. I'll…

920
00:31:58,852 --> 00:32:01,653
I'll work it off somehow.

921
00:32:01,653 --> 00:32:03,048
[The citizens' request has been granted]
It really can't be helped.

922
00:32:03,048 --> 00:32:04,226
Please sleep inside tonight.

923
00:32:04,226 --> 00:32:06,228
- Thank you! Thank you so much!
- As long as there's space.

924
00:32:06,228 --> 00:32:08,361
[Thank you, Your Highness]
Thank you!

925
00:32:08,361 --> 00:32:09,294
He...

926
00:32:09,294 --> 00:32:10,762
[My savior, Prince Shin Dong]
Saved our lives!

927
00:32:10,762 --> 00:32:12,234
He saved us.

928
00:32:12,234 --> 00:32:13,527
- Hurry and sleep.
- Oh, yeah.

929
00:32:13,527 --> 00:32:15,237
- Is the Commoner sleeping here?
- No, I'm…

930
00:32:15,237 --> 00:32:16,601
- This is his spot.
- Oh, really?

931
00:32:16,601 --> 00:32:17,636
This is my spot.

932
00:32:17,636 --> 00:32:19,039
[Commoner will sleep beside the prince's bed]
Thank you.

933
00:32:19,039 --> 00:32:21,006
Go find out first.

934
00:32:21,006 --> 00:32:23,042
[The paupers head out to find a room]
Thank you!

935
00:32:23,042 --> 00:32:24,371
Get some rest.

936
00:32:24,371 --> 00:32:26,373
Goodbye!

937
00:32:27,082 --> 00:32:30,168
[Will they find a place to sleep tonight…?]
Where are we supposed to go?

938
00:32:30,544 --> 00:32:33,172
[Meanwhile, in the peaceful NCTZ's room]

939
00:32:35,758 --> 00:32:38,192
[The bed is way too short]

940
00:32:38,192 --> 00:32:41,028
Do you just want to
share the bed with me?

941
00:32:41,028 --> 00:32:43,055
[Worried about the youngest sleeping cramped up]
Is it comfortable? You okay?

942
00:32:43,055 --> 00:32:44,516
I mean, I'm okay.

943
00:32:44,516 --> 00:32:47,267
But if we share a bed,
I think you'll be uncomfortable.

944
00:32:47,267 --> 00:32:48,735
[As expected, the cool guy from Chicago]
I'm fine.

945
00:32:48,735 --> 00:32:50,445
Not a big deal.

946
00:32:51,369 --> 00:32:55,540
I'm really fine with it,
but I'm just worried about one thing.

947
00:32:55,540 --> 00:32:57,279
- I kind of…
- Toss and twirl?

948
00:32:57,279 --> 00:32:58,035
Twist and turn?

949
00:32:58,035 --> 00:32:59,920
- Turn and toss?
- Kind of.

950
00:33:00,814 --> 00:33:02,215
[It's not like you're gonna hug me…]
It's okay.

951
00:33:02,215 --> 00:33:04,051
It's not like you'll hug me while you sleep.

952
00:33:04,051 --> 00:33:06,455
So what are you gonna do?
Are you gonna come on the bed?

953
00:33:06,455 --> 00:33:07,789
[Should I?]

954
00:33:08,458 --> 00:33:11,268
[The commoner gets a bed upgrade]

955
00:33:11,658 --> 00:33:15,095
Now that I'm a prince,
it's nice to even have time for a face mask.

956
00:33:15,095 --> 00:33:18,394
Paupers only get
the humidifying masks at this hour.

957
00:33:18,394 --> 00:33:21,435
[Thinking back on their dinner earlier]
So, about dinner earlier…

958
00:33:21,435 --> 00:33:22,732
Since it's the last day,

959
00:33:22,732 --> 00:33:26,607
I thought we'd just mess around
for about 10 minutes and then eat together.

960
00:33:26,607 --> 00:33:29,119
But after seeing that
the paupers didn't get anything…

961
00:33:29,119 --> 00:33:30,711
Seriously, wow…!

962
00:33:30,711 --> 00:33:33,514
What's fun about this show is…

963
00:33:33,514 --> 00:33:36,276
I'm not really competitive.

964
00:33:36,276 --> 00:33:39,930
But here, I don't want to lose.

965
00:33:39,930 --> 00:33:41,086
Just think about it.

966
00:33:41,086 --> 00:33:43,158
[Always doing my best]
When we were in Luxor…

967
00:33:43,158 --> 00:33:44,525
That was insane.

968
00:33:44,525 --> 00:33:47,441
I was kind of moved then.

969
00:33:47,441 --> 00:33:50,265
I actually ran a bit that day
because of you.

970
00:33:50,265 --> 00:33:51,098
- Oh, really?
- Yeah.

971
00:33:51,098 --> 00:33:53,626
I was pretty serious about it.

972
00:33:53,626 --> 00:33:55,611
[Johnny & Ji Sung's Pillow Talk Show]
But when you're alone,

973
00:33:55,611 --> 00:33:57,198


974
00:33:57,604 --> 00:33:58,966
[The conversation topic]
Do I react when I'm alone?

975
00:33:58,966 --> 00:34:00,467
[Do you react when you're alone?]
Yeah, you don't, right?

976
00:34:00,467 --> 00:34:02,722
You don't, right? You don't?

977
00:34:02,722 --> 00:34:04,867
[NCT 127 member]
But someone like Doyoung…

978
00:34:04,867 --> 00:34:06,346
does when he's alone.

979
00:34:06,346 --> 00:34:07,447
Oh?

980
00:34:07,447 --> 00:34:09,010
[Wait a minute…]
Do I do that too…?

981
00:34:09,416 --> 00:34:10,617
[Yes, you do. A lot]
Nice!

982
00:34:10,617 --> 00:34:12,085
It's an emergency…

983
00:34:12,085 --> 00:34:13,947
This is legendary...

984
00:34:13,947 --> 00:34:15,322
I don't do it.

985
00:34:15,322 --> 00:34:18,560
But these days,
no matter what it is,

986
00:34:18,560 --> 00:34:20,158
I try to enjoy it more.

987
00:34:20,158 --> 00:34:21,660
And honestly, when you do that,

988
00:34:21,660 --> 00:34:23,982
- it hits you so much harder.
- I agree. I felt it too.

989
00:34:23,982 --> 00:34:25,346
[Making an effort to enjoy something
makes it more memorable]

990
00:34:26,459 --> 00:34:28,869
When I heard
we were coming to Egypt,

991
00:34:28,869 --> 00:34:31,805
I contemplated for about 10 minutes.

992
00:34:31,805 --> 00:34:32,949
I'm really glad I came.

993
00:34:32,949 --> 00:34:34,993
- You're glad you came?
- Yeah.

994
00:34:34,993 --> 00:34:36,786
But…

995
00:34:36,786 --> 00:34:40,879
This was truly a proper trip, in a way.

996
00:34:40,879 --> 00:34:43,348
More than just visiting the Temple,

997
00:34:43,348 --> 00:34:45,953
- we actually played a game at the Temple.
- We played a game.

998
00:34:45,953 --> 00:34:47,120
So,

999
00:34:47,120 --> 00:34:49,287
even if people came here to travel,
they can't experience it like we did.

1000
00:34:49,287 --> 00:34:53,994
[A trip made special by enjoying the moment]
- That's true. - That's why we enjoyed it so much.

1001
00:34:53,994 --> 00:34:55,976
I think it's gonna stick
with me for a long time.

1002
00:34:56,396 --> 00:34:57,631
[Next topic]
So, I kind of

1003
00:34:57,631 --> 00:34:59,350
[Johnny's quirky trait]
have a bit of a unique thing going on.

1004
00:34:59,350 --> 00:35:00,298
What is it?

1005
00:35:00,298 --> 00:35:02,669
[I, Johnny, enjoy the struggle]
I kinda enjoy going through hardships.

1006
00:35:02,669 --> 00:35:07,872
- There's this thrill after the struggle ends
- Right, that's right.

1007
00:35:07,872 --> 00:35:11,311
Life… It makes me feel like I'm alive.

1008
00:35:12,546 --> 00:35:15,246
Since everyone's struggling here…

1009
00:35:15,246 --> 00:35:18,570
But I also like that
we're all suffering together.

1010
00:35:18,570 --> 00:35:20,909
I totally get what you mean.

1011
00:35:21,555 --> 00:35:23,154
[Severe memory distortion underway]
I think I'm kind of weird, actually.

1012
00:35:23,154 --> 00:35:25,256
- It makes us feel like a team, you know?
- Yeah.

1013
00:35:25,256 --> 00:35:27,661
Hey, but don't you think
we all have good chemistry together?

1014
00:35:27,661 --> 00:35:29,463
I just hoped it would be fun.

1015
00:35:29,463 --> 00:35:35,631
I couldn't imagine
what it'd be like from the lineup alone.

1016
00:35:37,204 --> 00:35:40,739
I still remember how awkward
I was on the first day.

1017
00:35:40,739 --> 00:35:42,941
[It felt so good to see a familiar face…]
But when you showed up,

1018
00:35:42,941 --> 00:35:45,412
I was so happy to see you.

1019
00:35:45,412 --> 00:35:46,613
It put my mind at ease.

1020
00:35:46,613 --> 00:35:48,625
That's true for me too.

1021
00:35:49,526 --> 00:35:52,069
Are you also the closest with
the NCT DREAM members?

1022
00:35:52,069 --> 00:35:54,653
I'm really the closest
with the members.

1023
00:35:54,653 --> 00:35:56,623
I'm like that too.

1024
00:35:56,623 --> 00:35:59,193
[The real reason he suddenly asked]
This thought suddenly crossed my mind.

1025
00:35:59,193 --> 00:36:02,370
We got close really fast.

1026
00:36:02,370 --> 00:36:03,289
Right?

1027
00:36:03,289 --> 00:36:05,299
[The secret?]
I figured it out.

1028
00:36:05,299 --> 00:36:07,034
It's because we went
through hardships together.

1029
00:36:07,034 --> 00:36:08,544
We struggled together,
and we overcame it together.

1030
00:36:08,544 --> 00:36:09,655
Those kinds of things are really…

1031
00:36:09,655 --> 00:36:10,642
[The conversation continues in the NCT room]

1032
00:36:11,171 --> 00:36:12,988
- It was fun, right?
- Yeah, it was fun.

1033
00:36:12,988 --> 00:36:14,474
[Prince Shin Dong's room
is getting ready for bed too]

1034
00:36:14,474 --> 00:36:15,843
(Knock)

1035
00:36:15,843 --> 00:36:17,611
Yes?

1036
00:36:17,611 --> 00:36:18,912
[The pauper citizens reappear]
Hello!

1037
00:36:18,912 --> 00:36:20,615
- Why?
- Why are you here?

1038
00:36:20,615 --> 00:36:22,983
They said there are no rooms available.

1039
00:36:22,983 --> 00:36:24,117
Let me just come in for now.

1040
00:36:24,117 --> 00:36:26,354
[The prince receives them with grace again]
Yes, yes, come on in.

1041
00:36:26,354 --> 00:36:28,731
It's fine. It's really fine.

1042
00:36:28,731 --> 00:36:29,666
- Is it okay?
- Yeah.

1043
00:36:29,666 --> 00:36:31,651
- Then Yo Han and I will…
- Yes.

1044
00:36:31,651 --> 00:36:35,154
[Then let's share a bed]
Right next to Shin Dong…!

1045
00:36:36,196 --> 00:36:38,131
- We'll just try lying down for a moment!
- Go ahead. Lie down.

1046
00:36:38,131 --> 00:36:39,464
[Let's go to bed together]
We'll just try lying here.

1047
00:36:39,464 --> 00:36:40,369
Go ahead, lie down.

1048
00:36:40,369 --> 00:36:42,037
- This is my spot, though.
- Yeah, right here.

1049
00:36:42,037 --> 00:36:44,205
[The burly citizens approach from both sides]
Wait, this bed actually fits us all?

1050
00:36:44,205 --> 00:36:44,998
It does.

1051
00:36:44,998 --> 00:36:46,333
[Three people lie down with no problem]
It fits, wow!

1052
00:36:46,333 --> 00:36:48,006
- This is nice.
- Can't we sleep like this?

1053
00:36:48,006 --> 00:36:48,811
All cozy and snug?

1054
00:36:48,811 --> 00:36:50,008
[We're actually quite close now]

1055
00:36:50,008 --> 00:36:51,379
Hey, this bed is seriously nice.

1056
00:36:51,379 --> 00:36:52,714
No, really.

1057
00:36:52,714 --> 00:36:55,282
[Allowing his citizens to share his bed]
Yeah, we can just sleep like this.

1058
00:36:55,282 --> 00:36:56,550
- For real?
- Yeah.

1059
00:36:56,550 --> 00:36:58,216
The two of them ended up
lying down on both sides.

1060
00:36:58,216 --> 00:37:01,386
But it was actually
way comfier than I expected.

1061
00:37:01,386 --> 00:37:03,390
[Special permission granted to save face]
I should protect my image at least.

1062
00:37:03,390 --> 00:37:06,193
So I told them both to sleep there.

1063
00:37:06,193 --> 00:37:09,122
[Teuk Dong Yo's 3-person slumber party]
So the three of us ended up sharing one bed.

1064
00:37:09,122 --> 00:37:11,065
Like, how can you sleep?

1065
00:37:11,065 --> 00:37:13,065
[Win-win]
There's no way you could sleep outside tonight.

1066
00:37:13,065 --> 00:37:14,968
[The prince saved the paupers' lives]
I went out here for a brief second.

1067
00:37:14,968 --> 00:37:17,280
The wind is blowing too hard.
It's too cold.

1068
00:37:19,640 --> 00:37:21,208
This won't do, Ji Sung.

1069
00:37:21,208 --> 00:37:22,743
I need to sleep like a prince
one last time.

1070
00:37:22,743 --> 00:37:25,475
[Since you're sleeping here, turn off the lights]
Let's turn off the lights.

1071
00:37:27,648 --> 00:37:31,360
[His first-ever prince experience ends]
Turns out, I was a prince all this time.

1072
00:37:37,489 --> 00:37:39,636
- Wow, this is crazy.
- Why?

1073
00:37:39,636 --> 00:37:42,071
[Clearly visible with the lights off]

1074
00:37:43,348 --> 00:37:45,761
With the lights off, this is crazy!

1075
00:37:46,601 --> 00:37:48,411
What's this? We turned off
the lights to sleep, and what is this?

1076
00:37:48,411 --> 00:37:50,888
- I wanna open the door, though.
- Let's go outside!

1077
00:37:52,203 --> 00:37:55,075
[Just like that, they get ready to stargaze]

1078
00:37:55,075 --> 00:37:56,618
[Bang!]

1079
00:37:57,778 --> 00:38:00,740
[He must've hit the glass door]
You hit the glass.

1080
00:38:03,635 --> 00:38:05,493
[Gotta see the stars even if it hurts]

1081
00:38:05,493 --> 00:38:07,121
Let's go out!

1082
00:38:08,331 --> 00:38:10,331
[Be right back]
Just stepping out for a sec!

1083
00:38:11,126 --> 00:38:14,420
[The two in black
and white hoodies step out quietly]

1084
00:38:16,631 --> 00:38:19,175
[They vanish out of sight]

1085
00:38:19,175 --> 00:38:21,011
I lay down to sleep when this guy was

1086
00:38:21,011 --> 00:38:23,555
[Chatting nonstop after stargazing]
looking at the stars, so we stepped out.

1087
00:38:23,555 --> 00:38:25,281
But the stars were so visible, so…

1088
00:38:26,808 --> 00:38:28,101
"Let's head into the desert."

1089
00:38:28,101 --> 00:38:32,280
[The Romantics made it all the way to the dunes]
So we went over there and back.

1090
00:38:33,022 --> 00:38:35,733
[Showing off the photos they took]

1091
00:38:37,585 --> 00:38:39,838
Honestly, it was amazing.

1092
00:38:39,838 --> 00:38:41,489
That day was just perfect.

1093
00:38:41,489 --> 00:38:44,700
I chatted with Johnny for a bit,
and then we went to see the stars.

1094
00:38:44,700 --> 00:38:46,277
A moment like this
might never happen again,

1095
00:38:46,277 --> 00:38:48,920
[A night full of great memories]
so it felt really special, and full of fun.

1096
00:38:49,563 --> 00:38:52,167
[Teuk Dong Yo are making
another unforgettable memory]

1097
00:38:52,167 --> 00:38:53,543
Can we sleep now?

1098
00:38:53,543 --> 00:38:56,770
Oh, is this really gonna be okay?

1099
00:38:56,770 --> 00:38:58,639
[The last night quietly fades away]
Should I turn off the lights, Shin Dong?

1100
00:38:58,639 --> 00:39:00,441
Please turn off the lights.

1101
00:39:08,057 --> 00:39:11,661
[The last day in Egypt]

1102
00:39:12,996 --> 00:39:16,708
[Johnny appears with a sagging style
first thing in the morning]

1103
00:39:19,569 --> 00:39:24,281
[He's here to enjoy
a relaxing cup of morning coffee]

1104
00:39:26,950 --> 00:39:31,205
[A morning coffee
to go with the morning Red Sea]

1105
00:39:38,754 --> 00:39:42,800
[While he charges up
on caffeine and romantic vibes]

1106
00:39:44,986 --> 00:39:47,972
[Teuk Dong Yo greet
the morning in a shocking state]

1107
00:39:49,198 --> 00:39:53,412
[Waking up refreshed with cries of pain]

1108
00:39:53,412 --> 00:39:56,530
Sleeping in the middle is so uncomfortable.

1109
00:39:56,530 --> 00:39:59,397
If I lean this way, there's a person.
If I lean that way, there's another.

1110
00:39:59,397 --> 00:40:00,632
[Sandwiched between the paupers]

1111
00:40:00,632 --> 00:40:04,572
Why does it feel like when I'm the prince,
I don't get that prince experience?

1112
00:40:04,572 --> 00:40:06,157
This is "ALL or NOTHING",

1113
00:40:06,157 --> 00:40:08,909
but it feels more like,
"NOTHING or NOTHING".

1114
00:40:08,909 --> 00:40:10,143
[Meanwhile, the real pauper is super satisfied]
I was so happy.

1115
00:40:10,143 --> 00:40:11,929
It was spacious, really spacious.

1116
00:40:11,929 --> 00:40:14,795
I turned a bit in my sleep,

1117
00:40:14,795 --> 00:40:18,102
and right next to me
was a super soft cushion.

1118
00:40:18,102 --> 00:40:19,270
Shin Dong.

1119
00:40:19,837 --> 00:40:22,215
[Lee Teuk's very own cushion]
At least you weren't lonely.

1120
00:40:22,215 --> 00:40:24,131
The bed's warm.

1121
00:40:24,925 --> 00:40:27,094
[Even doubles as a giant heat pack]
It could be because I'm warm.

1122
00:40:27,094 --> 00:40:29,071
Because I'm a warm-hearted guy.

1123
00:40:29,071 --> 00:40:30,797
[The final day that makes you homesick]
I want to go home.

1124
00:40:30,797 --> 00:40:32,770
We're leaving today.

1125
00:40:34,434 --> 00:40:36,604
Oh, Lee Teuk.

1126
00:40:36,604 --> 00:40:38,648
Open the curtain.
I'm curious what it looks like.

1127
00:40:38,648 --> 00:40:42,693
[Everyone wakes up with the sunlight]
Whoa, it's way too bright!

1128
00:40:44,403 --> 00:40:45,697
[Opening the curtains reveals…]

1129
00:40:45,697 --> 00:40:48,658
[A breathtaking view]

1130
00:40:50,618 --> 00:40:53,371
[The refreshing Red Sea under the morning sun]

1131
00:40:54,372 --> 00:40:56,624
[A morning gift from Giftun Island]

1132
00:40:56,624 --> 00:41:00,128
The water moving makes
it feel like the boat's moving.

1133
00:41:00,128 --> 00:41:01,713
She's iconic.

1134
00:41:01,713 --> 00:41:02,794
Did the rest of the guys come in?

1135
00:41:02,794 --> 00:41:05,432
[Johnny has a scheduled NCT 127 video call]

1136
00:41:06,634 --> 00:41:10,101
[Briefly switching to day job mode]

1137
00:41:10,101 --> 00:41:11,338
Yes.

1138
00:41:11,338 --> 00:41:14,877
[First showing off the beautiful view]
I'll show it to you.

1139
00:41:16,176 --> 00:41:19,752
[Video call topic: New comeback song]
Let's listen to it separately and meet up!

1140
00:41:20,915 --> 00:41:25,652
[Sincerely listening to the new song]

1141
00:41:28,953 --> 00:41:32,971
[The song must be a really exciting one]

1142
00:41:33,994 --> 00:41:36,372
[NCT 127 Taeyong]
Your energy's so high, being abroad and all.

1143
00:41:37,207 --> 00:41:39,057
Honestly, right now,

1144
00:41:39,057 --> 00:41:41,644
the view I'm seeing is
making the song sound even better.

1145
00:41:41,644 --> 00:41:44,272
[Happily wrapped up the meeting
thanks to the view]

1146
00:41:46,456 --> 00:41:50,261
[NCTZ head over to Shin Dong's room]

1147
00:41:54,033 --> 00:41:55,282
Good morning!

1148
00:41:55,282 --> 00:41:57,072
Wait, why are you here?

1149
00:41:57,915 --> 00:41:59,649
[Unaware of last night's drama]
You guys don't know a thing!

1150
00:41:59,649 --> 00:42:01,314
Oh, wow.

1151
00:42:01,314 --> 00:42:02,699
[To NCTZ too]
So, yesterday,

1152
00:42:02,699 --> 00:42:06,043
these three were
pitching their tent over there.

1153
00:42:06,043 --> 00:42:10,573
[Sharing the long, disastrous tale]
The wind was just way too strong.

1154
00:42:10,573 --> 00:42:12,283
[The unbelievable collapse
of the pauper's house]

1155
00:42:12,283 --> 00:42:14,786
- So they had nowhere to sleep.
- Seriously?

1156
00:42:14,786 --> 00:42:16,120
They begged me to let them sleep here.

1157
00:42:16,120 --> 00:42:19,807
[So we ended up sharing the room]
So we slept here like this.

1158
00:42:22,306 --> 00:42:24,211
Seriously,

1159
00:42:24,211 --> 00:42:26,922
yesterday was the peak of pauper life.

1160
00:42:27,382 --> 00:42:29,885
[Even the Paupert is shocked]
We slept really comfortably.

1161
00:42:29,885 --> 00:42:33,430
[Time to gear up for today's adventure]
Get ready.

1162
00:42:34,722 --> 00:42:39,535
[What's the grand finale mission?]

1163
00:42:39,960 --> 00:42:42,796
[1 hour later]

1164
00:42:46,341 --> 00:42:47,801
[The six guys are dragged somewhere once again]
That yellow boat looks nice.

1165
00:42:47,801 --> 00:42:51,067
Hey, something feels off here.

1166
00:42:52,588 --> 00:42:55,075
[This time, a yellow boat appears]
Doesn't it feel like it's more than just a boat?

1167
00:42:55,075 --> 00:42:58,045
Right? I feel like there's a catch.

1168
00:42:58,045 --> 00:43:00,151
I'm getting nervous.

1169
00:43:01,672 --> 00:43:03,281
Honestly, I'm a little scared…

1170
00:43:03,281 --> 00:43:04,785
[Suspicious]
Something's…

1171
00:43:04,785 --> 00:43:06,651
Everything is bolted down here.

1172
00:43:06,651 --> 00:43:09,489
Why is there an emergency exit here?

1173
00:43:09,489 --> 00:43:11,365
Does it drop down below or something?

1174
00:43:11,365 --> 00:43:14,410
[Suspicious about everything until the end]
Why would it drop below?

1175
00:43:14,995 --> 00:43:17,033
It wouldn't go down, right…?

1176
00:43:21,568 --> 00:43:24,404
[The final one]
The status missions are all done now.

1177
00:43:24,404 --> 00:43:25,536
That's right.

1178
00:43:25,536 --> 00:43:27,174
[No more missions]
No more for accommodations and things…

1179
00:43:27,174 --> 00:43:28,775
- Oh, they're done.
- There's no more.

1180
00:43:28,775 --> 00:43:30,475
You have something, though.

1181
00:43:30,475 --> 00:43:32,688
- If we didn't, you wouldn't do anything at all.
- That's true.

1182
00:43:32,688 --> 00:43:34,378
[Stating the obvious]
Please let us do some sightseeing!

1183
00:43:34,378 --> 00:43:38,519
We've prepared a reward
that you'll love more than anything else.

1184
00:43:38,519 --> 00:43:41,121
- More than anything else…?!
- Wow, what could it be?

1185
00:43:41,121 --> 00:43:43,490
Letting us eat the fish we catch?

1186
00:43:43,490 --> 00:43:45,957
- Why would we eat what we catch?
- But I am starving.

1187
00:43:45,957 --> 00:43:50,382
For now, just relax and enjoy the ride.

1188
00:43:50,382 --> 00:43:52,497
I'm so done with the boats.

1189
00:43:52,497 --> 00:43:57,004
If I'm being completely honest,
I want to stop getting blasted by the wind.

1190
00:43:57,004 --> 00:43:59,237
The wind blows too much.

1191
00:43:59,237 --> 00:44:00,304
[Before the whining worsens]
We've been traveling too much.

1192
00:44:00,304 --> 00:44:01,472
Can we just go somewhere, just us…

1193
00:44:01,472 --> 00:44:05,376
[The boat takes off]
It's moving, it's moving!

1194
00:44:05,376 --> 00:44:07,134
¡Vamos!

1195
00:44:07,134 --> 00:44:08,532
Let's go!

1196
00:44:11,883 --> 00:44:15,856
So a huge group is
supposed to ride this together, like that.

1197
00:44:15,856 --> 00:44:17,691
(Hello)
Oh, actually, we have a huge group too.

1198
00:44:17,691 --> 00:44:18,840
You have to wave like this.

1199
00:44:18,840 --> 00:44:21,242
You're supposed to wave back
for things like this.

1200
00:44:25,140 --> 00:44:26,733
[Greeting back with a dance]

1201
00:44:26,733 --> 00:44:28,669
Oh, there's a dancer over there!

1202
00:44:28,669 --> 00:44:30,771
Shouldn't we show them
what we got too?

1203
00:44:30,771 --> 00:44:34,041
Ji Sung, you danced
when you went to the club.

1204
00:44:34,041 --> 00:44:35,901
- A club?
- Yeah.

1205
00:44:35,901 --> 00:44:38,078
- You went to a club?
- A club?

1206
00:44:38,078 --> 00:44:41,014
- He went to an Egyptian club.
- That word just sounds so…

1207
00:44:41,014 --> 00:44:43,281
You're really into clubbing, huh?

1208
00:44:43,281 --> 00:44:46,137
- You're showing us so many new sides of yourself.
- I've never been to one in my life...

1209
00:44:46,137 --> 00:44:48,712
[Except you totally have]

1210
00:44:49,082 --> 00:44:52,359
[That night on Day 3 when you went all out]

1211
00:44:52,359 --> 00:44:55,596
In front of the cruise, oh…

1212
00:44:55,596 --> 00:44:57,689
I was dancing with the little kids then.

1213
00:44:57,689 --> 00:45:00,434
You danced with little kids at the club?

1214
00:45:00,434 --> 00:45:04,569
[Getting a kick out of teasing the youngest]
That's way too scandalous!

1215
00:45:04,569 --> 00:45:07,441
- This is bad.
- This is bad! You're gonna end up in the news!

1216
00:45:07,441 --> 00:45:09,694
[Innocent]
But it's really true.

1217
00:45:09,694 --> 00:45:12,371
- Why did the sea suddenly turn so blue?
- Probably because it's deep.

1218
00:45:12,371 --> 00:45:14,742
- It must be pretty deep around here.
- Oh, you're right.

1219
00:45:14,742 --> 00:45:16,692
It's crystal clear over there.

1220
00:45:18,127 --> 00:45:20,725
By any chance,
is anyone here a good swimmer?

1221
00:45:21,164 --> 00:45:22,322
A good swimmer…?

1222
00:45:22,322 --> 00:45:23,824
I can swim.

1223
00:45:23,824 --> 00:45:25,659
- Do you enjoy it?
- I do.

1224
00:45:25,659 --> 00:45:28,429
I can go in, but it's important to know
if my feet can touch the bottom.

1225
00:45:28,429 --> 00:45:29,930
Can you go in if you can't touch the ground?

1226
00:45:29,930 --> 00:45:31,282
I can't.

1227
00:45:31,965 --> 00:45:33,161
Will you go in if you have a life jacket?

1228
00:45:33,161 --> 00:45:34,476
Oh, if I have a life jacket, I can go in.

1229
00:45:34,476 --> 00:45:36,069
[But asking about swimming skills means…]

1230
00:45:36,069 --> 00:45:38,105
We're going there.

1231
00:45:38,105 --> 00:45:39,715
We're going snorkeling, huh?

1232
00:45:39,715 --> 00:45:40,754
- Yes, that's right.
- We are!

1233
00:45:40,754 --> 00:45:42,275
[Bingo!]

1234
00:45:42,907 --> 00:45:43,874
We are!

1235
00:45:43,874 --> 00:45:45,638
I should've practiced before coming.

1236
00:45:45,638 --> 00:45:49,224
[The Red Sea, the mecca for snorkeling]

1237
00:45:50,701 --> 00:45:53,813
[The real reason they came here
will be revealed shortly]

1238
00:45:53,813 --> 00:45:56,449
What kind of fish live in the Red Sea?

1239
00:45:56,449 --> 00:45:57,608
Tropical fish.

1240
00:45:57,608 --> 00:46:00,507
Then it must be warm!
Tropical fish means warm water.

1241
00:46:00,507 --> 00:46:03,085
They're not tropical fish because
it has the word "heat" in the name.

1242
00:46:03,085 --> 00:46:03,961
Then?

1243
00:46:03,961 --> 00:46:05,732
If it's warm… wouldn't they get cooked?

1244
00:46:05,732 --> 00:46:07,386
But they're tropical fish.

1245
00:46:07,386 --> 00:46:09,870
They usually live in warm water
around 20 to 30 degrees.

1246
00:46:09,870 --> 00:46:11,514
[Forget about yesterday's freezing cold]
See? I told you I was right.

1247
00:46:11,514 --> 00:46:13,246
[Tropical fish live in 20-30℃ water]
20 to 30 degrees for tropical fish.

1248
00:46:13,246 --> 00:46:15,250
- The water?
- That's really warm!

1249
00:46:15,250 --> 00:46:18,011
[Master of random facts]
Oh! It is!

1250
00:46:18,011 --> 00:46:20,579
But let's say we went in the water…

1251
00:46:20,579 --> 00:46:21,913
What if we get bitten?

1252
00:46:21,913 --> 00:46:23,247
Bitten by what?

1253
00:46:23,247 --> 00:46:25,052
- By piranhas.
- Piranhas?

1254
00:46:25,052 --> 00:46:26,596
[Master of random facts]

1255
00:46:26,596 --> 00:46:28,856
Then it'd go viral and be good.

1256
00:46:28,856 --> 00:46:30,724
[Getting bitten guarantees #1 Trending]
First of all, piranhas aren't saltwater fish.

1257
00:46:30,724 --> 00:46:32,393
- Oh really?
- Yes.

1258
00:46:32,393 --> 00:46:34,025
[Then]
What if a shark shows up?

1259
00:46:34,025 --> 00:46:35,829
- A shark?
- Yeah.

1260
00:46:35,829 --> 00:46:37,995
Perhaps that imagination of yours

1261
00:46:37,995 --> 00:46:40,986
is what's making you scared
of going into the water.

1262
00:46:40,986 --> 00:46:44,779
When I was a kid, I went to Jeju Island.

1263
00:46:44,779 --> 00:46:49,968
I was swimming alone, and I drifted away
to a spot where I couldn't reach the ground.

1264
00:46:49,968 --> 00:46:52,596
- I was thrashing around in fear…
- Yeah, I totally get that.

1265
00:46:52,596 --> 00:46:56,183
- and I couldn't do anything but sink.
- You can't do anything.

1266
00:46:56,183 --> 00:46:57,885
How did you get back?

1267
00:46:57,885 --> 00:46:59,451
I don't remember exactly, but at the time,

1268
00:46:59,451 --> 00:47:02,119
I was sinking, swallowing the water like crazy…

1269
00:47:02,119 --> 00:47:03,423
Seriously!

1270
00:47:03,423 --> 00:47:05,275
It's so vivid in my memory.

1271
00:47:05,275 --> 00:47:08,762
You just said you don't remember,
so what's so vivid?

1272
00:47:08,762 --> 00:47:10,761
- You're right.
- What does that mean?

1273
00:47:10,761 --> 00:47:12,743
[Such a contradictory person]
Just roll with it.

1274
00:47:12,743 --> 00:47:14,535
- So, my memory…
- That's strange.

1275
00:47:14,535 --> 00:47:17,246
That's like saying "Loudly whisper."

1276
00:47:17,246 --> 00:47:19,816
[Flustered]
I'm just saying!

1277
00:47:19,816 --> 00:47:21,774
Please just say, "Oh, really?"

1278
00:47:21,774 --> 00:47:23,736
Oh, really?

1279
00:47:24,111 --> 00:47:27,464
[Oh, yes, I see!]
So, this is Egypt!

1280
00:47:28,649 --> 00:47:29,706
I have no idea where we're headed.

1281
00:47:29,706 --> 00:47:32,147
[Before they know it,
they're in the middle of the Red Sea]

1282
00:47:32,147 --> 00:47:34,263
I feel like we're almost there.

1283
00:47:34,263 --> 00:47:35,356
I think we're here.

1284
00:47:35,356 --> 00:47:36,390
This is it!

1285
00:47:36,390 --> 00:47:38,042
[Arrived at the destination]
Alright, everyone, we're here.

1286
00:47:38,042 --> 00:47:40,257
- For real?
- Wow, this is the place?

1287
00:47:40,257 --> 00:47:44,398
First, before we explain
what today's mission is…

1288
00:47:44,398 --> 00:47:47,713
This boat is
actually a famous tourist attraction.

1289
00:47:47,713 --> 00:47:48,735
And its special feature is…

1290
00:47:48,735 --> 00:47:50,463
[A boat with a surprise]
right underneath the boat.

1291
00:47:50,463 --> 00:47:52,272
- Underneath?
- Yes.

1292
00:47:52,272 --> 00:47:54,308
[Is this a semi-submarine?]
Is it a submarine, by any chance?

1293
00:47:54,308 --> 00:47:55,926
[Correct]
That's right.

1294
00:47:55,926 --> 00:47:56,827
No way!

1295
00:47:56,827 --> 00:47:59,013
- That's amazing!
- We should've gone in earlier! It's so cold!

1296
00:47:59,013 --> 00:48:01,324
[Hurghada, embracing the Red Sea]

1297
00:48:02,391 --> 00:48:05,870
[Full of mysterious wonders]

1298
00:48:06,355 --> 00:48:09,273
[A pristine underwater world]

1299
00:48:09,791 --> 00:48:13,903
[And you get to enjoy it from inside the boat]

1300
00:48:14,292 --> 00:48:15,697
[Moving to the unexpected space below]
Wow, amazing!

1301
00:48:15,697 --> 00:48:18,174
Wow, incredible!

1302
00:48:20,868 --> 00:48:24,671
[Revealing the submerged area]

1303
00:48:24,671 --> 00:48:26,590
- Oh, it's so cold! So cold!
- Really?

1304
00:48:31,687 --> 00:48:35,107
[When you climb down
the stairs of the semi-submarine,]

1305
00:48:35,625 --> 00:48:38,802
[there are underwater windows on both sides]

1306
00:48:39,995 --> 00:48:44,041
[that open up to a natural aquarium right outside]

1307
00:48:46,310 --> 00:48:49,393
- Wow! Wow!
- This is epic!

1308
00:48:49,393 --> 00:48:50,330
[So cool]

1309
00:48:50,330 --> 00:48:52,233
There are tropical fish down there.

1310
00:48:57,471 --> 00:48:58,836
Hey Ji Sung!

1311
00:48:58,836 --> 00:48:59,973
It's a real jellyfish!

1312
00:48:59,973 --> 00:49:01,441
Where? Where?

1313
00:49:01,441 --> 00:49:04,178
Wow, they're real fish!

1314
00:49:04,178 --> 00:49:05,824
Wow, this is insane!

1315
00:49:05,824 --> 00:49:07,239
I've never seen anything like this!

1316
00:49:07,239 --> 00:49:09,637
- This is crazy.
- Wow, this is amazing!

1317
00:49:09,637 --> 00:49:11,310
[Everyone's hyped by the scene before their eyes]
This is incredible!

1318
00:49:11,310 --> 00:49:12,670
It's really the wild. The wild.

1319
00:49:12,670 --> 00:49:15,455
[Super close-up]
Wow, what is this?

1320
00:49:15,455 --> 00:49:18,565
[Completely losing track of time]
It's big, it's big, it's big!

1321
00:49:18,565 --> 00:49:20,689
Wow, there are so many fish over there!

1322
00:49:20,689 --> 00:49:21,965
Wow, this is totally worth seeing.

1323
00:49:21,965 --> 00:49:24,515
[The kidults are completely captivated]
Wow, we definitely had to come see this.

1324
00:49:24,515 --> 00:49:26,183
This is so great.

1325
00:49:26,183 --> 00:49:27,382
Seriously so great.

1326
00:49:27,382 --> 00:49:30,910
We weren't seeing them in an aquarium,
but from under the sea.

1327
00:49:30,910 --> 00:49:33,487
After going right
in the middle of the Red Sea.

1328
00:49:33,487 --> 00:49:36,022
It was genuinely breathtaking.

1329
00:49:36,022 --> 00:49:39,606
Like "I can't believe we're seeing this."
It was so cool.

1330
00:49:39,606 --> 00:49:44,505
Being able to see fish
without even going in the water…!

1331
00:49:45,244 --> 00:49:47,654
It was a whole new experience for me.

1332
00:49:47,654 --> 00:49:50,224
It's only possible
because the water is so clear here.

1333
00:49:50,224 --> 00:49:51,501
Oh, that's true.

1334
00:49:51,501 --> 00:49:53,503
Are they curious about us too?

1335
00:49:53,503 --> 00:49:55,629
I bet they're like, "What on earth is this?"

1336
00:49:55,629 --> 00:49:59,967
Whoa, what the heck!
That scared me!

1337
00:49:59,967 --> 00:50:01,481
[Laughing over the smallest things]
It just shot right up, huh?

1338
00:50:01,481 --> 00:50:03,237
- The two of them!
- Yeah, the two of them!

1339
00:50:03,237 --> 00:50:05,372
They were so dark
that it really startled me.

1340
00:50:05,372 --> 00:50:07,374
I feel like a kid again.

1341
00:50:07,374 --> 00:50:09,139
Wow, but this is really cool.

1342
00:50:09,139 --> 00:50:11,270
I don't think I can hold back.
I need to go in there!

1343
00:50:11,270 --> 00:50:13,891
I need to get in the water right now!

1344
00:50:14,681 --> 00:50:15,608
Wow, if we really go in…

1345
00:50:15,608 --> 00:50:17,181
- Hey, what's that?
- It'd be crazy.

1346
00:50:17,181 --> 00:50:19,837
[Completely fallen for the Red Sea]
It's really cool watching the waves above too.

1347
00:50:19,837 --> 00:50:21,151
The waves are really strong.

1348
00:50:21,151 --> 00:50:23,491
[Really enjoyed the semi-submarine tour]
So pretty.

1349
00:50:23,491 --> 00:50:24,967
Seriously beautiful

1350
00:50:24,967 --> 00:50:26,535
Amazing!

1351
00:50:26,535 --> 00:50:27,898
Amazing, it was really amazing.

1352
00:50:27,898 --> 00:50:30,228
We enjoyed everything!

1353
00:50:30,228 --> 00:50:32,208
Let's get going now!

1354
00:50:32,208 --> 00:50:34,701
What is this?

1355
00:50:34,701 --> 00:50:37,337
- Wow…
- What is this?

1356
00:50:37,337 --> 00:50:40,966
[Came back from the tour and found a safe]

1357
00:50:42,142 --> 00:50:44,553
Isn't this totally my specialty again?

1358
00:50:44,553 --> 00:50:46,839
[What is this?]
Hey, don't just push buttons. It won't work.

1359
00:50:46,839 --> 00:50:48,752
That was seriously amazing. Wow.

1360
00:50:48,752 --> 00:50:49,983
Oh, looks like there's something more.

1361
00:50:49,983 --> 00:50:52,597
Let's just sit down and listen, like before.

1362
00:50:52,597 --> 00:50:55,281
This is the grand finale mission

1363
00:50:55,281 --> 00:50:56,682
to wrap things up

1364
00:50:56,682 --> 00:50:59,143
- on our trip in Egypt.
- Wow. No way…

1365
00:50:59,143 --> 00:51:02,593
The moment you've all been waiting for…

1366
00:51:02,593 --> 00:51:03,698
6 to 0!

1367
00:51:03,698 --> 00:51:05,450
- Is this a team challenge?
- 6 to 0!

1368
00:51:05,450 --> 00:51:08,068
It's a team challenge!

1369
00:51:08,068 --> 00:51:11,306
Everyone succeeds together,

1370
00:51:11,306 --> 00:51:13,373
or everyone fails together.

1371
00:51:13,373 --> 00:51:15,375
[Truly bound together by fate]
Please!

1372
00:51:15,375 --> 00:51:16,410
And…

1373
00:51:16,410 --> 00:51:18,556
- You're probably curious about the reward.
- Yes

1374
00:51:18,556 --> 00:51:21,591
Looking at our schedule,
once we're done with today,

1375
00:51:21,591 --> 00:51:22,950
[Back to Cairo for the flight to Korea!]
we'll head over to Cairo

1376
00:51:22,950 --> 00:51:26,019
- and fly back to Seoul from there, right?
- Yes.

1377
00:51:26,019 --> 00:51:27,554
We'll be taking a big charter bus.

1378
00:51:27,554 --> 00:51:30,257
[Hurghada to Cairo]
It takes about five and a half to six hours.

1379
00:51:30,257 --> 00:51:31,558
[6-hour bus ride]
[1-hour flight]

1380
00:51:31,558 --> 00:51:33,223
That's way too long, way too long!

1381
00:51:33,223 --> 00:51:35,812
So! We're putting domestic
flight tickets on the line!

1382
00:51:35,812 --> 00:51:37,690
[Reward for success:
1-hour domestic flight tickets]

1383
00:51:37,690 --> 00:51:39,800
That's huge.

1384
00:51:39,800 --> 00:51:43,229
You probably know
since you saw it in the back.

1385
00:51:43,229 --> 00:51:46,139
[The safe holds the company card]
The company card's inside there.

1386
00:51:46,139 --> 00:51:48,240
[Flight tickets will be purchased if successful]
If we succeed, we're the only ones flying?

1387
00:51:48,240 --> 00:51:50,119
If you succeed, only you will be flying.

1388
00:51:52,413 --> 00:51:54,457
- Thank you.
- Okay, so…

1389
00:51:54,457 --> 00:51:55,916
The mission title is

1390
00:51:55,916 --> 00:51:59,903
"The Mermaid Prince's Math Class".

1391
00:52:01,255 --> 00:52:04,969
[The Mermaid Prince dives underwater]
Remember the windows you looked through earlier?

1392
00:52:04,969 --> 00:52:06,928
If you dive down
and get close to them,

1393
00:52:06,928 --> 00:52:11,465
[Random numbers will appear on the semi-sub window]
we're gonna show you some numbers.

1394
00:52:11,465 --> 00:52:12,933
[After seeing the numbers, shout them out]
After seeing the numbers,

1395
00:52:12,933 --> 00:52:16,103
come back up to the surface
and share what the numbers were.

1396
00:52:16,103 --> 00:52:17,939
With the numbers you received,

1397
00:52:17,939 --> 00:52:20,841
you must multiply them in your head!

1398
00:52:20,841 --> 00:52:24,995
[The calculated product is the code to the safe!]

1399
00:52:25,846 --> 00:52:28,282
The time limit is 15 minutes.

1400
00:52:28,282 --> 00:52:30,270
- 15 minutes?
- Yes.

1401
00:52:30,948 --> 00:52:33,287
I'm really bad with numbers.
I'm weak with numbers!

1402
00:52:33,287 --> 00:52:34,714
[Whether weak or strong, it's a teamwork mission]
It's a team mission.

1403
00:52:34,714 --> 00:52:36,291
The team that goes in the water!

1404
00:52:36,291 --> 00:52:37,667
Within your team,

1405
00:52:37,667 --> 00:52:40,627
the Physical Team
will handle the swimming.

1406
00:52:40,627 --> 00:52:43,923
And the Brain Team
will handle the math calculations.

1407
00:52:43,923 --> 00:52:46,099
- You have to split into those teams.
- Okay.

1408
00:52:46,099 --> 00:52:48,602
First, is anyone definitely on the Physical Team?

1409
00:52:48,602 --> 00:52:49,870
I like swimming.

1410
00:52:49,870 --> 00:52:51,138
- Oh, okay.
- Johnny.

1411
00:52:51,138 --> 00:52:53,440
I need to go into the Red Sea at least once!

1412
00:52:53,440 --> 00:52:55,251
Okay, anyone else?

1413
00:52:56,298 --> 00:53:00,647
[No one's stepping up]
No one? Johnny's the only one so far?

1414
00:53:00,647 --> 00:53:03,305
Okay, then Team Brain!
Raise your hands!

1415
00:53:03,305 --> 00:53:03,927
(Hand shoots up) (Hand shoots up) (Hand shoots up)
I'm…
(Hesitates)
I'm definitely…

1416
00:53:04,502 --> 00:53:05,445
(Hand shoots up)

1417
00:53:05,445 --> 00:53:06,888
If I had to pick between the two,
it's gotta be Brain.

1418
00:53:06,888 --> 00:53:08,822
Brain, definitely Brain.

1419
00:53:08,822 --> 00:53:10,257
I actually prepared for a PhD.

1420
00:53:10,257 --> 00:53:12,426
[G University
(International Commerce / PhD program dropout)]

1421
00:53:12,426 --> 00:53:14,828
It is possible with just one person
on the Physical Team.

1422
00:53:14,828 --> 00:53:16,630
- Since he can just keep looking at it.
- Right?

1423
00:53:16,630 --> 00:53:18,588
[15 minutes]
- But it'll take longer. - That's right.

1424
00:53:18,588 --> 00:53:19,833
[Need at least 2 people on the Physical Team to win]
We need at least 2 people.

1425
00:53:19,833 --> 00:53:22,577
So anyone who can go in the water,
please step up.

1426
00:53:22,577 --> 00:53:24,304
(Hmm)
You never swam in the ocean, huh?

1427
00:53:24,304 --> 00:53:26,106
Then, you can't.

1428
00:53:26,106 --> 00:53:29,810
I'm not really Team Brain or Team Physical.
It's very iffy.

1429
00:53:29,810 --> 00:53:34,557
But I did take a swimming class in college.

1430
00:53:34,557 --> 00:53:36,683
I think I got a C+.

1431
00:53:36,683 --> 00:53:39,052
[I guess it's up to me (C+)]
Looks like I'm the one for the job.

1432
00:53:39,052 --> 00:53:42,656
It's definitely better
for Lee Teuk to stay on top.

1433
00:53:42,656 --> 00:53:45,850
[Need more brains to calculate]
The more people on top, the faster we calculate.

1434
00:53:46,423 --> 00:53:49,280
Don't worry about that.
Don't worry about the calculations.

1435
00:53:49,280 --> 00:53:52,996
[Physical Team]
[Brain Team]

1436
00:53:52,996 --> 00:53:54,732
[A brief time to change]
Okay, everyone, warm up.

1437
00:53:54,732 --> 00:53:55,869
We've got this, we've got this!

1438
00:53:55,869 --> 00:53:58,456
[While they change]
Let's practice our multiplication.

1439
00:53:58,456 --> 00:54:01,041
Keep memorizing the times table.

1440
00:54:01,041 --> 00:54:03,377
[Multiplication practice led by Captain Shin Dong]
72x8.

1441
00:54:03,377 --> 00:54:04,687
72x8.

1442
00:54:04,687 --> 00:54:06,547
- 8x2=16
- That's right.

1443
00:54:06,547 --> 00:54:09,016
[Stuck on the next step]
72.

1444
00:54:09,016 --> 00:54:11,652
[72x8]
574.

1445
00:54:11,652 --> 00:54:13,599
It's actually 576!

1446
00:54:13,599 --> 00:54:15,856
[It gets tricky with 3-digit numbers]
Okay, so this is how you do it.

1447
00:54:15,856 --> 00:54:17,049
Let's do it like this.

1448
00:54:17,049 --> 00:54:18,221
[Each person takes a unit's place to multiply]
You multiply the ones place.

1449
00:54:18,221 --> 00:54:20,060
You multiply the tens place.

1450
00:54:20,060 --> 00:54:22,238
[One person adds it all up]
Then, we'll pick someone who adds everything up.

1451
00:54:22,238 --> 00:54:23,376
Then it'll be easy.

1452
00:54:23,376 --> 00:54:25,298
[505x3=?]
505x3!

1453
00:54:25,298 --> 00:54:26,500
[Ones place]
15.

1454
00:54:26,500 --> 00:54:27,401
[Tens place]
0.

1455
00:54:27,401 --> 00:54:28,669
[Hundreds place]
15.

1456
00:54:28,669 --> 00:54:31,530
So what's the answer? It's 1515.
That's how you do it.

1457
00:54:31,530 --> 00:54:32,532
[Much easier]
Just think of it that way.

1458
00:54:32,532 --> 00:54:34,157
Shin Dong, that's so good.

1459
00:54:34,157 --> 00:54:36,218
- Are you in STEM?
- No, I'm in the humanities.

1460
00:54:36,218 --> 00:54:37,344
[Just classic Captain Shin Dong brilliance]
You're in the humanities?

1461
00:54:37,344 --> 00:54:39,441
Let's do it like this!
It works, right?

1462
00:54:39,441 --> 00:54:41,044
It's easy to multiply
a unit place at a time, right?

1463
00:54:41,044 --> 00:54:43,450
If it's like this,
I think I could even do it.

1464
00:54:43,450 --> 00:54:45,048
Time for the times table!

1465
00:54:45,048 --> 00:54:46,987
[Let's test your multiplication skills]
Time for the times table!

1466
00:54:46,987 --> 00:54:48,130
[7x6=?]
- What's 7x6? - 30...

1467
00:54:48,130 --> 00:54:48,956
- Huh?
- You're going in the water?

1468
00:54:48,956 --> 00:54:50,174
[Stop stalling and jump in]
It's 42, 42!

1469
00:54:50,174 --> 00:54:52,343
Too late! You gotta say it right away!

1470
00:54:52,343 --> 00:54:55,191
- We can do it if we do it like this, right?
- Yeah, we got this.

1471
00:54:56,597 --> 00:54:59,191
But what's really weird was…

1472
00:54:59,679 --> 00:55:02,603
I don't know what came over me, but…

1473
00:55:02,603 --> 00:55:03,871
[Multiplying single digits]
It's just multiplication,

1474
00:55:03,871 --> 00:55:05,754
[15 minutes for this?]
but they're giving us 15 minutes?

1475
00:55:06,691 --> 00:55:09,375
[Not your standard numbers]
These might not be normal numbers.

1476
00:55:09,375 --> 00:55:12,136
[Are there separate Egyptian numbers?!]
They could give us numbers in Egyptian numerals.

1477
00:55:12,679 --> 00:55:13,823
[20 minutes earlier, during break time]
I'm so hungry.

1478
00:55:13,823 --> 00:55:14,995
I'm hungry.

1479
00:55:14,995 --> 00:55:16,483
[Whining]
I'm so hungry!

1480
00:55:16,483 --> 00:55:18,352
- Do you need snacks?
- Yes!

1481
00:55:18,352 --> 00:55:20,037
[Egyptian snacks given to WANGGEOZ]
Please give us some!

1482
00:55:20,037 --> 00:55:21,455
Oreo!

1483
00:55:21,455 --> 00:55:24,333
All the food wrappers
had Arabic numerals on them.

1484
00:55:24,333 --> 00:55:25,292
Oreo!

1485
00:55:25,292 --> 00:55:26,438
Sure enough,

1486
00:55:26,438 --> 00:55:28,052
[The snack was printed with Arabic numerals]
it had 8 cookies inside, with 2 extra.

1487
00:55:28,052 --> 00:55:31,131
So it said there are 10 inside in Arabic numerals.

1488
00:55:31,131 --> 00:55:33,025
And on the side, there was a plus sign

1489
00:55:33,025 --> 00:55:35,736
followed by some Egyptian hieroglyphs.

1490
00:55:35,736 --> 00:55:37,512
[Egyptian numbers written on the right side]

1491
00:55:37,512 --> 00:55:41,033
[The Western Arabic numerals we all know]

1492
00:55:41,033 --> 00:55:44,878
[Meanwhile, Eastern Arabic numerals
that look like hieroglyphs]

1493
00:55:44,878 --> 00:55:48,488
[Egypt uses Eastern Arabic numerals]

1494
00:55:48,488 --> 00:55:50,918
[Looking closely]

1495
00:55:50,918 --> 00:55:52,850
I think this is the number 2.

1496
00:55:52,850 --> 00:55:54,571
[Curiosity sparks his instincts]
Is this 2? Or is this 8?

1497
00:55:54,571 --> 00:55:56,281
We had a conversation about this.

1498
00:55:56,281 --> 00:55:57,287
But?

1499
00:55:57,287 --> 00:55:59,871
It's just multiplication,
but they're giving us 15 minutes.

1500
00:55:59,871 --> 00:56:00,918
[The mission time was suspiciously long]
Huh?

1501
00:56:00,918 --> 00:56:02,137
[It hits him]
I've got a bad feeling about this.

1502
00:56:02,137 --> 00:56:03,827
[Instinct kicks in]
Let's memorize this!

1503
00:56:03,827 --> 00:56:06,467
[Urgently gathering all the members]
Lee Teuk, let's gather around!

1504
00:56:06,467 --> 00:56:07,575
(Crowding around)
Let's huddle up.

1505
00:56:07,575 --> 00:56:09,556
Let's come up with a plan!

1506
00:56:09,556 --> 00:56:11,837
From what I can tell right now,

1507
00:56:11,837 --> 00:56:14,902
[Instinct activated]
the passcode probably isn't a long number.

1508
00:56:14,902 --> 00:56:17,244
It's suspicious that they're
giving us 15 minutes for it.

1509
00:56:17,244 --> 00:56:18,930
[Now that you mention it, it's sus]
Right? Totally suspicious.

1510
00:56:18,930 --> 00:56:20,180
So the thing is,

1511
00:56:20,180 --> 00:56:22,224
it might not be the Arabic numbers we know.

1512
00:56:22,224 --> 00:56:24,718
Did you see the numbers
on the side while eating the OREO earlier?

1513
00:56:24,718 --> 00:56:25,736
I told you, right?

1514
00:56:25,736 --> 00:56:28,655
[Ji Sung also remembers the Egyptian numbers]
It looks like a 7, but it's actually a 2.

1515
00:56:28,655 --> 00:56:30,254
[A plausible theory]
It could be those numbers.

1516
00:56:30,254 --> 00:56:32,092
- Ancient numbers?
- Yeah.

1517
00:56:32,092 --> 00:56:33,360
[But…]
Then…

1518
00:56:33,360 --> 00:56:36,129
[We don't know Egyptian numbers?]
Then… Then we…

1519
00:56:36,129 --> 00:56:38,533
(What do we do?)
We don't know those numbers.

1520
00:56:38,533 --> 00:56:41,498
[Quickly search ON]
Oh my.

1521
00:56:41,498 --> 00:56:42,870
[Stunned by numbers they've never seen before]
How are we supposed to know this?

1522
00:56:42,870 --> 00:56:45,507
So Egypt has its own numbers.

1523
00:56:48,242 --> 00:56:49,859
Wow, I can see it!

1524
00:56:49,859 --> 00:56:51,603
- Wow, so cool!
- Why?

1525
00:56:51,603 --> 00:56:52,715
(What do you see?)
Look at this!

1526
00:56:52,715 --> 00:56:54,181
[On screen]
I didn't notice looking at it like this.

1527
00:56:54,181 --> 00:56:56,178
[If you rotate it…]
But if you look at it this way…

1528
00:56:56,178 --> 00:56:57,871
[Turning it around]
It says "1, 2, 3" like this!

1529
00:56:57,871 --> 00:57:00,012
- Oh, what?
- Right? Isn't it cool?

1530
00:57:00,012 --> 00:57:01,811
If you rotate it, you can see it.

1531
00:57:01,811 --> 00:57:05,717
[Egyptian numbers that look like hieroglyphs]

1532
00:57:05,717 --> 00:57:07,987
[When rotated vertically,]

1533
00:57:09,230 --> 00:57:11,691
[the digits look vaguely familiar]

1534
00:57:12,166 --> 00:57:14,901
[0 and 1 look the most similar]

1535
00:57:14,901 --> 00:57:18,531
It's 2 and 3, and if you rotate it,
it looks like 2 and 3.

1536
00:57:18,531 --> 00:57:21,559
And 4 is a flipped 3.

1537
00:57:21,559 --> 00:57:23,787
And 5? It's the letter O.

1538
00:57:23,787 --> 00:57:26,472
We pronounce 5 as "O" in Korean, so 5 is O.

1539
00:57:26,472 --> 00:57:29,227
And we memorized "7" as 6.

1540
00:57:29,227 --> 00:57:31,752
And next, "V" is 7.

1541
00:57:31,752 --> 00:57:33,862
We make a 7 like this with our hands, right?
So, it's 7.

1542
00:57:33,862 --> 00:57:36,190
And then, when it's flipped, it's 8.

1543
00:57:36,190 --> 00:57:38,150
And 9 looks the same.

1544
00:57:38,150 --> 00:57:39,192
Hey, memorize this!

1545
00:57:39,192 --> 00:57:40,925
[Memorizing Eastern Arabic numbers with mnemonics]
I made everyone do it 3 times!

1546
00:57:40,925 --> 00:57:42,195
"Hey, what is it?"

1547
00:57:42,195 --> 00:57:43,797
"What does it look like?"
"Write it starting from 1."

1548
00:57:43,797 --> 00:57:46,435
[Trusting Shin Dong's instinct, everyone starts memorizing]
For example, I'll call 4 "a flipped 3"!

1549
00:57:46,435 --> 00:57:47,395
I'll say it like this!

1550
00:57:47,395 --> 00:57:50,671
- It's 2. It's 2.
- 4 is a flipped 3.

1551
00:57:50,671 --> 00:57:51,672
So…

1552
00:57:51,672 --> 00:57:53,273
[Meticulously memorizing to prepare for the challenge]
4 is different, and 5…

1553
00:57:53,273 --> 00:57:55,609
If I say "7," it'll be confusing,
so I'll call it the Korean letter "gi-yeok."

1554
00:57:55,609 --> 00:57:56,626
Gi-yeok.

1555
00:57:56,626 --> 00:57:58,112
[Meanwhile, someone just stays still like a clam]
6 is gi-yeok.

1556
00:57:58,112 --> 00:57:59,366
5 is O.

1557
00:57:59,366 --> 00:58:01,307
Oh, 5 is O!

1558
00:58:01,307 --> 00:58:03,097
We absolutely have to pull this off, so…

1559
00:58:03,097 --> 00:58:05,115
I have to sit this one out!

1560
00:58:05,115 --> 00:58:08,019
I'm completely useless in that situation.

1561
00:58:08,387 --> 00:58:10,917
[His self-awareness is insane (positive)]
I'm just dead weight.

1562
00:58:10,917 --> 00:58:12,826
- 5 is O.
- Okay, I'll say 5 is O.

1563
00:58:12,826 --> 00:58:15,459
You just have to look
and tell us what it looks like.

1564
00:58:15,459 --> 00:58:16,709
- Just describe what you see to us.
- Got it, gi-yeok.

1565
00:58:16,709 --> 00:58:18,432
[The Mermaid Princes promise
to describe what they see]

1566
00:58:18,432 --> 00:58:20,868
[Will Captain Shin Dong's hunch be right?]

1567
00:58:20,868 --> 00:58:23,563
[The Mermaid Prince's Math Class]
We'll begin the Mermaid Prince's Math Class.

1568
00:58:23,563 --> 00:58:25,939
[Brain power]
I've got a feeling it might be 2026.

1569
00:58:25,939 --> 00:58:28,275
[Physical Power]
First, let's check how many digits there are.

1570
00:58:28,275 --> 00:58:30,040
- 2, 3…
- That's right.

1571
00:58:30,040 --> 00:58:30,953
[The final mission with all six members]
Flipped 4.
That's right.

1572
00:58:31,854 --> 00:58:34,450
[Using brains and brawn to the max]
One person solves, and the other remembers it.

1573
00:58:34,450 --> 00:58:37,050
[Clear the final mission]

1574
00:58:37,050 --> 00:58:39,111
I'll wrap this up in 5 minutes flat.

1575
00:58:39,111 --> 00:58:40,519
[I'm ready]
It's perfect.

1576
00:58:41,088 --> 00:58:42,281
[Following Captain Shin Dong, they get serious]
3x1=3, 3x2=6, 3x3=9…

1577
00:58:42,281 --> 00:58:43,290
3x4=12.

1578
00:58:43,290 --> 00:58:44,424
3x5=15.

1579
00:58:44,424 --> 00:58:45,926
[3x8=?]
3x8?

1580
00:58:45,926 --> 00:58:47,027
56?

1581
00:58:47,027 --> 00:58:48,762
Huh? Wait!

1582
00:58:48,762 --> 00:58:50,514
[Not ready for the 3 times tables...?]
Ji Sung seems a bit rusty.

1583
00:58:50,514 --> 00:58:51,874
You're kinda making me nervous.

1584
00:58:51,874 --> 00:58:52,608
[Uh…um…uh, uh…]

1585
00:58:52,608 --> 00:58:53,726
I'm a bit weak
with the 3 times table…

1586
00:58:53,726 --> 00:58:54,668
[This was filmed under expert
supervision and following safety guidelines]

1587
00:58:54,668 --> 00:58:55,836
Oh, why am I suddenly…

1588
00:58:55,836 --> 00:58:59,873
[The Mermaid Princes are ready to dive in]
Why am I suddenly feeling nervous about this?

1589
00:58:59,873 --> 00:59:02,109
[The mathematicians are ready to solve the problems]
Let's get on the plane!

1590
00:59:02,109 --> 00:59:04,056
["ALL or NOTHING" Final Mission]

1591
00:59:05,646 --> 00:59:06,737
[GAME START]
Here we go!

1592
00:59:06,737 --> 00:59:11,018
- Let's go, let's go
- We've got this!

1593
00:59:11,018 --> 00:59:13,787
[Mermaid Prince Johnny dives in]

1594
00:59:13,787 --> 00:59:15,471
- Did he go right in?
- Hey, Johnny's already down there.

1595
00:59:15,471 --> 00:59:18,423
[Diving fearlessly into the Red Sea]
He went already?

1596
00:59:20,544 --> 00:59:22,212
[Smitten]
Johnny's so cool.

1597
00:59:24,198 --> 00:59:26,550
[Descending below the submarine]

1598
00:59:26,550 --> 00:59:29,620
[Cutting through the waves without hesitation]

1599
00:59:32,539 --> 00:59:35,409
[Visible through the window are…]

1600
00:59:35,409 --> 00:59:37,476
[Eastern Arabic numerals?!]

1601
00:59:39,672 --> 00:59:42,466
[Johnny ascends immediately]

1602
00:59:43,628 --> 00:59:44,910
- Shin Dong!
- Huh?

1603
00:59:44,910 --> 00:59:47,955
What you predicted was spot on!

1604
00:59:47,955 --> 00:59:49,432
What is that?!

1605
00:59:49,432 --> 00:59:52,364
The Eastern Arabic numbers!
The Eastern Arabic numbers!

1606
00:59:52,364 --> 00:59:53,926
[We...]

1607
00:59:53,926 --> 00:59:56,171
[practiced for this!!!]

1608
00:59:56,827 --> 01:00:00,097
[Our instincts were spot on]
We were right. They weren't ordinary numbers.

1609
01:00:00,097 --> 01:00:02,503
I thought I should hurry
back up and tell the others.

1610
01:00:02,503 --> 01:00:03,652
Shin Dong!

1611
01:00:03,652 --> 01:00:04,840
[What you were thinking about]
It's the symbol you were talking about!

1612
01:00:04,840 --> 01:00:05,635
[was right]

1613
01:00:05,635 --> 01:00:08,354
[Joy]
Yes! We got this!

1614
01:00:08,354 --> 01:00:10,473
[Will they remember without getting mixed up?]

1615
01:00:11,478 --> 01:00:13,176
[The first number is "gi-yeok"]
It's gi-yeok! It's gi-yeok!

1616
01:00:13,176 --> 01:00:14,056
Gi-yeok? Gi-yeok?

1617
01:00:14,056 --> 01:00:15,916
(What number was "gi-yeok" again?)
Gi-yeok? What was gi-yeok?

1618
01:00:15,916 --> 01:00:17,069
No, no, no! Gi-yeok!

1619
01:00:17,069 --> 01:00:19,586
[I'll call 6 "gi-yeok"]
I'll call it "gi-yeok." If I say "7," it'll be confusing.

1620
01:00:19,586 --> 01:00:20,713
[Using "gi-yeok" for the number 6]
Oh, gi-yeok!

1621
01:00:20,713 --> 01:00:22,340
- I'll call it "gi-yeok."
- Gi-yeok.

1622
01:00:22,340 --> 01:00:23,216
6 is gi-yeok.

1623
01:00:23,216 --> 01:00:24,341
- 7!
- No!

1624
01:00:24,341 --> 01:00:24,934
[ctrl+c]
No, it's 6! 6! 6! 6! 6! 6!

1625
01:00:24,934 --> 01:00:26,318
[ctrl+v]
6! 6! 6! 6! 6! 6!

1626
01:00:26,318 --> 01:00:27,390
[Smoothly locked in the first number]
6! 6! 6! 6! 6! 6!

1627
01:00:27,390 --> 01:00:28,429
6! 6! 6!

1628
01:00:28,429 --> 01:00:30,781
[Off to the next number!]

1629
01:00:34,326 --> 01:00:35,661
(Waving around)

1630
01:00:37,671 --> 01:00:39,946
[Spotted an upside-down "V"]

1631
01:00:41,175 --> 01:00:42,748
- V! V!
- V?

1632
01:00:42,748 --> 01:00:43,794
[Passed the wrong information]
V? What was V again?

1633
01:00:43,794 --> 01:00:45,069
- V! V!
- 8!

1634
01:00:45,069 --> 01:00:46,180
Hold on, hold on.

1635
01:00:46,180 --> 01:00:47,514
- 7x8=56.
- Oh! 7! 7! 7! 6x7!

1636
01:00:47,514 --> 01:00:49,116
[Trusting the Mermaid Princes and starting mental math]
6x7?

1637
01:00:49,116 --> 01:00:50,283
[The ones place answer]
What's 6x7?

1638
01:00:50,283 --> 01:00:51,585
[6x7=42]
6×7=42!

1639
01:00:51,585 --> 01:00:53,120
[The one just now was a flipped V]
The one earlier was a flipped V!

1640
01:00:53,120 --> 01:00:54,154
Flipped V!

1641
01:00:54,154 --> 01:00:55,556
[Fortunately, they correct the error quickly]
The one earlier was a flipped V!

1642
01:00:55,556 --> 01:00:57,791
The second one is a flipped V?
It's 8! 8!

1643
01:00:57,791 --> 01:00:59,126
[6x8=?]
6x8.

1644
01:00:59,126 --> 01:00:59,793
[Current numbers acquired: 6, 8]
42!

1645
01:00:59,793 --> 01:01:01,528
[42]
6x8.

1646
01:01:01,528 --> 01:01:02,439
6x8, 6x8 is…

1647
01:01:02,439 --> 01:01:03,897
- 6x8=48.
- That's right!

1648
01:01:03,897 --> 01:01:06,100
[Oh…I'm getting nervous…]
Hey, something's off. Something's off.

1649
01:01:08,011 --> 01:01:11,389
[The Mermaid Prince
dives down to check the third number]

1650
01:01:16,560 --> 01:01:19,329
(Flailing)

1651
01:01:19,329 --> 01:01:21,415
(Charades)

1652
01:01:21,415 --> 01:01:22,950
[Megaphone ON]
O! O! O!

1653
01:01:22,950 --> 01:01:24,585
[Current numbers acquired: 6, 8, 5]
Hey, 48x5!

1654
01:01:24,585 --> 01:01:26,520
- O? O?
- 48 times… One person at a time!

1655
01:01:26,520 --> 01:01:27,554
[Ones place]
40.

1656
01:01:27,554 --> 01:01:28,697
[Tens place]
20.

1657
01:01:28,697 --> 01:01:30,966
- 240! 240! 240!
- 240!

1658
01:01:30,966 --> 01:01:31,992
[It's going smoothly]
This is how to do it!

1659
01:01:31,992 --> 01:01:32,885
6?

