7x7 is definitely 49.

1898
01:09:01,608 --> 01:09:02,817
- It's 49, right?
- Yeah.

1899
01:09:02,817 --> 01:09:04,378
And then you multiply it by 4.

1900
01:09:04,378 --> 01:09:05,742
- 9x4=36.
- 36.

1901
01:09:05,742 --> 01:09:07,697
[Wait a sec...]
Then it's 196.

1902
01:09:07,697 --> 01:09:09,289
No, wait! Hey!

1903
01:09:09,289 --> 01:09:11,084
Our math is wrong!

1904
01:09:11,084 --> 01:09:12,515
It should come out
to like 200-something?!

1905
01:09:12,515 --> 01:09:14,245
- Yeah, look.
- Oh, really? Our math is wrong?

1906
01:09:14,245 --> 01:09:15,204
[Spiraling again...]
7x7=49.

1907
01:09:15,204 --> 01:09:16,857
No, just take 49

1908
01:09:16,857 --> 01:09:18,025
and multiply it by 4.

1909
01:09:18,025 --> 01:09:19,601
- 4x9=36.
- That's right.

1910
01:09:19,601 --> 01:09:21,211
- 4x4=16.
- So then...

1911
01:09:21,211 --> 01:09:22,772
It's 206!

1912
01:09:22,772 --> 01:09:24,589
- Why is it 206?
- 49x4 is...

1913
01:09:24,589 --> 01:09:25,507
[Chills]
There's no way it's 200...?

1914
01:09:25,507 --> 01:09:26,696
[That number can't possibly come out...?]
4x4=16.

1915
01:09:26,696 --> 01:09:27,549
How could it be 200?

1916
01:09:27,549 --> 01:09:29,277
- Take the 200...
- It's 196. 196!

1917
01:09:29,277 --> 01:09:30,871
- Yeah, it's 196.
- It's 196.

1918
01:09:30,871 --> 01:09:33,073
- Just multiply 196 by 4.
- Times 4.

1919
01:09:33,073 --> 01:09:34,364
[6x4=24]
6x4=24.

1920
01:09:34,891 --> 01:09:35,534
Ah, 4x6...

1921
01:09:35,534 --> 01:09:36,836
- Is it not?
- With 194...

1922
01:09:36,836 --> 01:09:39,475
[Brain suddenly stops]

1923
01:09:39,475 --> 01:09:40,855
- 3.
- 4x5=20.

1924
01:09:40,855 --> 01:09:42,165
4x5=20!

1925
01:09:42,165 --> 01:09:43,479
Ah, 24! 24! Sorry!

1926
01:09:43,479 --> 01:09:44,551
[You said it correctly 10 seconds ago]
And multiply it by 4.

1927
01:09:44,551 --> 01:09:45,886
6x4=24.

1928
01:09:45,886 --> 01:09:46,787
[Mistakenly thinking he's wrong]
Did you mess up then?

1929
01:09:46,787 --> 01:09:48,409
- I messed up!
- Oh, really? 24. Okay!

1930
01:09:48,409 --> 01:09:50,175
[DAWN, you weren't wrong...]
24. Okay! 24.

1931
01:09:50,175 --> 01:09:52,659
- I was wrong, I was wrong.
- You were the one messing up.

1932
01:09:52,659 --> 01:09:53,468
[Tens place]
36!
Yeah, 36.

1933
01:09:54,461 --> 01:09:55,512
[Hundreds place]
Mine is 4.

1934
01:09:55,512 --> 01:09:56,452
Then...?
Oh, this is confusing.

1935
01:09:57,157 --> 01:09:59,629
784?
It's 784?

1936
01:09:59,629 --> 01:10:04,688
[Will this painfully calculated number be correct?]
Please let there be no more inside.

1937
01:10:06,923 --> 01:10:08,675
[It opened!]
Okay!

1938
01:10:08,675 --> 01:10:10,419
We got it! We got it!

1939
01:10:11,136 --> 01:10:12,546
Is it over?!

1940
01:10:12,546 --> 01:10:13,755
Did we get it?

1941
01:10:14,381 --> 01:10:17,451
[Let's hurry home
and make up for lost time...!]

1942
01:10:17,451 --> 01:10:18,660
Please, please!

1943
01:10:23,156 --> 01:10:24,649
[Excited]
Hey! Hey!

1944
01:10:24,649 --> 01:10:26,412
Quick! One more time!
One more time!

1945
01:10:27,828 --> 01:10:29,788
[Waaah, I'm a baby lock]

1946
01:10:30,176 --> 01:10:31,965
Ugh... Seriously, I...!

1947
01:10:31,965 --> 01:10:34,030
This is driving me crazy...

1948
01:10:34,030 --> 01:10:35,102
How many numbers is it?

1949
01:10:35,102 --> 01:10:36,395
- 4 numbers.
- 4 numbers.

1950
01:10:36,911 --> 01:10:39,246
[The Mermaid Princes who were
watching what was happening above]

1951
01:10:40,040 --> 01:10:42,475
[dive in at the same time]

1952
01:10:42,976 --> 01:10:46,530
When I went in a third time,
it became a mental battle at that point.

1953
01:10:46,530 --> 01:10:47,648
"I have to do this..."

1954
01:10:47,648 --> 01:10:49,812
That's when my muscles started getting sore...

1955
01:10:49,812 --> 01:10:51,635
[His energy started running out]
The waves kept crashing,

1956
01:10:51,635 --> 01:10:53,781
so I had to use even more energy.

1957
01:10:53,781 --> 01:10:56,603
- It must be so hard for Johnny.
- I seriously feel so bad!

1958
01:10:57,024 --> 01:10:58,688
- Flipped 7!
- Flipped 7!

1959
01:10:58,688 --> 01:10:59,701
If it's a Flipped 7, then it's 6.

1960
01:10:59,701 --> 01:11:01,715
- Flipped 7 is 6.
- Yeah, 6.

1961
01:11:01,715 --> 01:11:05,132
[Getting faster with repetition]

1962
01:11:05,132 --> 01:11:06,466
- Flipped V.
- Flipped V.

1963
01:11:06,466 --> 01:11:07,334
Flipped V?

1964
01:11:07,334 --> 01:11:08,886
- 8.
- 8?

1965
01:11:08,886 --> 01:11:09,820
8?
- 7x8!
- 7x8.

1966
01:11:10,637 --> 01:11:11,588
7x8=56!

1967
01:11:12,005 --> 01:11:13,302
[Literally a moment ago...]
Flipped 7!

1968
01:11:13,302 --> 01:11:14,048
If it's a flipped 7, then it's 6.

1969
01:11:14,048 --> 01:11:15,532
[After saying it was a 6]
Flipped 7 is 6.

1970
01:11:15,532 --> 01:11:16,117
8.

1971
01:11:16,117 --> 01:11:17,410
[They forgot again...]
8? 7x8.

1972
01:11:17,410 --> 01:11:18,536
7x8=56!

1973
01:11:19,146 --> 01:11:20,297
- 9.
- 9.

1974
01:11:20,297 --> 01:11:21,911
- 9 is 9!
- 56x9!

1975
01:11:21,911 --> 01:11:23,083
[Calculating with wrong numbers again...]
56x9...

1976
01:11:23,083 --> 01:11:24,751
- 9x6 is...
- 54.

1977
01:11:24,751 --> 01:11:25,686
6x9=54.

1978
01:11:25,686 --> 01:11:26,954
- 45.
- 45.

1979
01:11:26,954 --> 01:11:27,958
[ALL or NOTHING]
504

1980
01:11:27,958 --> 01:11:29,605
- 504?
- I still remember up to 504.

1981
01:11:29,605 --> 01:11:30,273
[ALL or SILLY]
504!

1982
01:11:30,273 --> 01:11:33,192
504, 504, 504,
504, 504, 504...

1983
01:11:34,228 --> 01:11:36,163
9 was the last one, right?

1984
01:11:36,697 --> 01:11:38,565
There's one more "siot."

1985
01:11:38,565 --> 01:11:41,163
[Yo Han suddenly says there's a Korean character?]
Our workload doubled because of him.

1986
01:11:41,735 --> 01:11:44,530
[Diving back in to re-check the numbers]

1987
01:11:46,673 --> 01:11:48,560
There are only 3 numbers, though?!

1988
01:11:48,560 --> 01:11:49,734
There are no more?

1989
01:11:49,734 --> 01:11:51,944
- There are only 3!
- There are only 3?

1990
01:11:51,944 --> 01:11:55,516
[The lock needs 4 numbers]

1991
01:11:55,516 --> 01:11:56,950
[There are only 3 numbers?]
There are no more? There are only 3?

1992
01:11:56,950 --> 01:11:58,785
Should we try 0-504? 0-504?

1993
01:11:58,785 --> 01:11:59,786
054…

1994
01:11:59,786 --> 01:12:00,621
[0504 / 5040]
0504.

1995
01:12:00,621 --> 01:12:03,257
[Trying with zeroes in the front and back]
There's gotta be a zero either in front or back.

1996
01:12:03,257 --> 01:12:05,087
- It's not, it's not.
- Then...

1997
01:12:05,087 --> 01:12:06,794
- Should we try the other way?
- The opposite way.

1998
01:12:06,794 --> 01:12:08,253
It's not opening.

1999
01:12:08,253 --> 01:12:10,697
Can you please check one more time?

2000
01:12:10,697 --> 01:12:13,633
[Prince Yo Han's on it]
Yo Han's really good at this now!

2001
01:12:14,050 --> 01:12:16,486
[Cutting through the current
and checking thoroughly]

2002
01:12:19,139 --> 01:12:20,506
- Hold on.
- Yeah.

2003
01:12:20,506 --> 01:12:21,622
Take your time!
Take your time!

2004
01:12:21,622 --> 01:12:22,663
[Yo Han's number: 8]
"Siot"!

2005
01:12:22,663 --> 01:12:23,226
"Siot"?

2006
01:12:23,226 --> 01:12:25,119
- Flipped V!
- Oh, flipped V!

2007
01:12:25,119 --> 01:12:25,678
And then...

2008
01:12:25,678 --> 01:12:26,938
[Yo Han's numbers: 8, 9]
9!

2009
01:12:26,938 --> 01:12:28,815
- 8, 9.
- 6x9=54.

2010
01:12:28,815 --> 01:12:30,041
[Yo Han's numbers: 8, 9, 8]
Flipped V!

2011
01:12:30,041 --> 01:12:30,668
Oh, it's 8, 9?
8x9=72!

2012
01:12:31,417 --> 01:12:32,986
[The numbers are different from Johnny's?]
8x9=72.

2013
01:12:32,986 --> 01:12:34,504
- And then?
- Flipped V!

2014
01:12:35,155 --> 01:12:37,198
[Going back to verify]

2015
01:12:37,198 --> 01:12:38,300
- It's like that?
- 8, 9, 8?

2016
01:12:38,300 --> 01:12:39,951
- Is it 8, 9, 8? 8, 9, 8?
- It's 8, 9, 8!

2017
01:12:39,951 --> 01:12:41,495
8x9?

2018
01:12:41,495 --> 01:12:44,289
[I'm pretty sure I saw it correctly...]

2019
01:12:45,164 --> 01:12:46,582
[Panicked]
Oh, Lee Teuk! Lee Teuk! Lee Teuk!

2020
01:12:46,582 --> 01:12:48,502
The first one!

2021
01:12:48,502 --> 01:12:50,070
- It's a sideways 3!
- Sideways 3?

2022
01:12:50,070 --> 01:12:52,272
It's 3! It's 3!

2023
01:12:52,272 --> 01:12:54,130
[The number Johnny confirmed]

2024
01:12:54,591 --> 01:12:56,301
[Shaped like a 3 on its side,]

2025
01:12:56,301 --> 01:12:57,819
[the number 3]

2026
01:12:58,511 --> 01:13:00,848
[But when he first saw the number]

2027
01:13:00,848 --> 01:13:02,949
- Flipped 7!
- Flipped 7!

2028
01:13:02,949 --> 01:13:05,719
[Mixing up the two numbers]

2029
01:13:05,719 --> 01:13:07,254
3-8-9!! 3-8-9!! Then...

2030
01:13:07,254 --> 01:13:08,534
[Recalculating with the new number]
What did we have at the beginning?

2031
01:13:08,534 --> 01:13:09,689
[Current numbers: 3, 8, 9]
Was it 7, 8, 9?

2032
01:13:09,689 --> 01:13:11,566
- No, it's not.
- It was 8x9=72.

2033
01:13:11,566 --> 01:13:12,325
Ugh... Why can't I remember this?

2034
01:13:12,325 --> 01:13:13,543
[Echoing]
3x9... Then it's...!

2035
01:13:13,543 --> 01:13:14,737
- Then it's 3...!
- Ugh, it's so noisy here…

2036
01:13:14,737 --> 01:13:16,697
- 9! What was it?
- Why is everyone loud here...?

2037
01:13:16,697 --> 01:13:17,999
- 3!
- 9!

2038
01:13:17,999 --> 01:13:19,157
[So chaotic...]
Flipped V!

2039
01:13:19,157 --> 01:13:20,367
[Echoing loudly]
3, 8, 9! 3, 8, 9!

2040
01:13:20,367 --> 01:13:21,743
3, 8, 9! 3, 8, 9!

2041
01:13:21,743 --> 01:13:23,036
3x8!!

2042
01:13:23,036 --> 01:13:26,456
3x8=24!

2043
01:13:26,456 --> 01:13:27,399
[Something's off…]
Is it 3, 8, 9?

2044
01:13:27,399 --> 01:13:28,625
Wasn't it 4 numbers earlier?

2045
01:13:28,625 --> 01:13:29,910
- Again!
- No, they said there were only 3!

2046
01:13:29,910 --> 01:13:30,644
Oh, but!

2047
01:13:30,644 --> 01:13:32,646
Why did Yo Han say it was 8, 9, 8...?

2048
01:13:32,646 --> 01:13:33,447
Why did he say 8, 9, 8?

2049
01:13:33,447 --> 01:13:35,474
[Happily clueless]
Why did he say 8, 9, 8?

2050
01:13:35,474 --> 01:13:37,007
3, 8, 9?

2051
01:13:37,007 --> 01:13:38,899
Please look one more time!
I'm sorry!

2052
01:13:38,899 --> 01:13:40,790
[Giving up...]
Something's wrong! It won't open.

2053
01:13:40,790 --> 01:13:43,182
- 1 minute left!
- There's only 1 minute left!

2054
01:13:44,024 --> 01:13:44,992
3x8 is...

2055
01:13:44,992 --> 01:13:46,309
- 8x9=72.
- 72.

2056
01:13:46,309 --> 01:13:47,952
What is this?

2057
01:13:50,464 --> 01:13:53,634
But I did make a mistake there.

2058
01:13:53,634 --> 01:13:56,569
I didn't see that
there was another number at the end.

2059
01:13:56,569 --> 01:13:58,830
[That number that caused all the confusion]

2060
01:14:02,009 --> 01:14:03,210
[What Johnny saw]
It's a sideways 3!

2061
01:14:03,210 --> 01:14:04,244
Flipped V!

2062
01:14:04,244 --> 01:14:05,234
9!

2063
01:14:05,234 --> 01:14:06,446
[What Yo Han saw]
"Siot"!

2064
01:14:06,446 --> 01:14:08,665
9! Reversed V!

2065
01:14:08,665 --> 01:14:11,084
[Just need to combine
everything they said together]

2066
01:14:11,084 --> 01:14:12,419
There's another flipped V!

2067
01:14:12,419 --> 01:14:14,215
- Another flipped V!
- See? See?

2068
01:14:14,988 --> 01:14:17,124
- 216! 216!
- Multiply 216 with...

2069
01:14:17,124 --> 01:14:18,650
[The value of 216x8 is the answer]
8!

2070
01:14:18,650 --> 01:14:19,791
6x8 is?

2071
01:14:19,791 --> 01:14:20,990
[Ones place]
6x8=48

2072
01:14:20,990 --> 01:14:22,016
[Tens place]
80!

2073
01:14:22,016 --> 01:14:23,137
Wait a sec, 80...

2074
01:14:23,137 --> 01:14:25,332
- So just 80...
- Yeah, just 80.

2075
01:14:25,332 --> 01:14:26,936
[Hundreds place]
16.

2076
01:14:28,101 --> 01:14:29,933
1886...?

2077
01:14:30,436 --> 01:14:32,146
You said it's 1200?

2078
01:14:32,146 --> 01:14:33,803
Okay, 30 seconds!

2079
01:14:33,803 --> 01:14:35,108
[Time's running out]
Let's try it again one more time.

2080
01:14:35,108 --> 01:14:36,343
6x8 is?

2081
01:14:36,343 --> 01:14:37,177
48.

2082
01:14:37,177 --> 01:14:38,478
[48+80]
80.

2083
01:14:38,478 --> 01:14:40,380
[48+80=128]
128! 128! What's yours, Lee Teuk?

2084
01:14:40,380 --> 01:14:41,481
I got 16!
2x8=16!

2085
01:14:41,481 --> 01:14:42,983
[128+1600=17...]
1, 7...

2086
01:14:42,983 --> 01:14:44,968
10!

2087
01:14:44,968 --> 01:14:46,247
- 9!
- 1, 7, what is it?

2088
01:14:46,247 --> 01:14:47,314
- 8!
- 48.

2089
01:14:47,314 --> 01:14:48,432
- 7!
- You're 8, right?

2090
01:14:48,432 --> 01:14:49,466
6!

2091
01:14:50,157 --> 01:14:52,101
5!

2092
01:14:52,101 --> 01:14:54,195
4!

2093
01:14:54,195 --> 01:14:55,571
3!

2094
01:14:55,571 --> 01:14:56,955
2!

2095
01:14:56,955 --> 01:14:58,463
1!

2096
01:14:58,463 --> 01:15:01,092
[Game Over]
It's not working!

2097
01:15:01,092 --> 01:15:03,237
[Bewildered]
It's not working!

2098
01:15:03,237 --> 01:15:05,005
Is it over?

2099
01:15:05,005 --> 01:15:06,973
The Mermaid Prince's Math Class.

2100
01:15:06,973 --> 01:15:07,924
Wait, wait. Just wait.

2101
01:15:07,924 --> 01:15:10,017
- The final mission...!
- Wait! Just wait!

2102
01:15:10,017 --> 01:15:12,270
[Mission Failed]
You have failed.

2103
01:15:12,894 --> 01:15:14,147
[This has to be a lie.....]

2104
01:15:14,147 --> 01:15:16,383
- Why isn't it right?
- Wait a minute.

2105
01:15:16,383 --> 01:15:18,626
[Can't let it go]
6x8=48, isn't it?

2106
01:15:18,626 --> 01:15:19,820
Yeah.

2107
01:15:19,820 --> 01:15:21,254
[The Mermaid Princes who worked the hardest]
You did so well!

2108
01:15:21,254 --> 01:15:22,697
- You really did!
- We're sorry!

2109
01:15:22,697 --> 01:15:23,840
No, no.

2110
01:15:23,840 --> 01:15:25,893
We're the ones
who couldn't calculate it.

2111
01:15:25,893 --> 01:15:27,928
Was multiplication always this hard?

2112
01:15:27,928 --> 01:15:28,995
Sit down, sit down.

2113
01:15:28,995 --> 01:15:30,663
I think it's warmer in the water.

2114
01:15:30,663 --> 01:15:32,306
Just sit here for now.

2115
01:15:32,306 --> 01:15:33,683
- How did it go?
- Are you okay?

2116
01:15:33,683 --> 01:15:35,477
- We... We couldn't do it.
- We failed, we failed.

2117
01:15:35,477 --> 01:15:36,470
- We failed.
- Really?

2118
01:15:36,470 --> 01:15:38,272
The numbers were right.

2119
01:15:38,272 --> 01:15:41,441
- We were such fools!!
- Why? What went wrong?

2120
01:15:41,441 --> 01:15:43,810
[Figured out the answer afterwards]
128+1600... Why?

2121
01:15:43,810 --> 01:15:45,245
Why couldn't I figure this out?

2122
01:15:45,245 --> 01:15:47,281
1728. I did this earlier, didn't I?

2123
01:15:47,281 --> 01:15:49,222
[Got really close to the answer]
We went with 48 earlier.

2124
01:15:49,222 --> 01:15:51,576
- Oh, we went with 48?
- Ugh, what an idiot move...!

2125
01:15:51,576 --> 01:15:54,536
[I'm such an idiot...]
I was such a fool...

2126
01:15:55,396 --> 01:15:56,523
Oh!

2127
01:15:57,291 --> 01:15:59,334
I was unlocking it the wrong way.

2128
01:15:59,726 --> 01:16:01,628
It presses down like this,

2129
01:16:01,628 --> 01:16:02,996
[Captain Shin Dong misunderstood the unlocking method]
so I thought you had to press and pull.

2130
01:16:02,996 --> 01:16:05,961
But because I pressed and pulled,
it didn't work. Such a fool!

2131
01:16:05,961 --> 01:16:07,481
[What a bummer]
Then we were right earlier.

2132
01:16:07,481 --> 01:16:08,868
You just had to pull it.

2133
01:16:09,343 --> 01:16:11,454
Customer, you worked so hard!

2134
01:16:11,839 --> 01:16:13,874
[Applause for the hard-working Mermaid Princes]
You two really worked hard.

2135
01:16:13,874 --> 01:16:15,208
- For real.
- It's such a shame, though!

2136
01:16:15,208 --> 01:16:17,644
Hey, I'm so sorry.
I'm really sorry.

2137
01:16:17,644 --> 01:16:21,348
To explain to the Physical Team
who worked hard down there,

2138
01:16:21,348 --> 01:16:24,613
the team up here
just couldn't do the math.

2139
01:16:24,613 --> 01:16:26,761
- Oh, were we wrong?
- You found all the right numbers.

2140
01:16:26,761 --> 01:16:28,055
[Reason for failure: Terrible math skills]
They just couldn't do the math.

2141
01:16:28,055 --> 01:16:29,819
Yeah, that's right.

2142
01:16:29,819 --> 01:16:32,058
I kept saying 4x6=26.

2143
01:16:32,058 --> 01:16:34,528
How is 4x6 even 26?

2144
01:16:34,528 --> 01:16:35,729
[Q. What caused the failure?]

2145
01:16:35,729 --> 01:16:37,130
The people up there!

2146
01:16:37,130 --> 01:16:39,933
6x4=24!
Even I know that!

2147
01:16:39,933 --> 01:16:42,769
[I'd be a brainiac with that too]
I got at least that much brain power.

2148
01:16:42,769 --> 01:16:45,613
Honestly, I felt kind of sorry as well, so…

2149
01:16:45,613 --> 01:16:48,199
[Just left feeling a little disappointed]
It just ended with "What a bummer."

2150
01:16:48,199 --> 01:16:49,597
But of course!

2151
01:16:49,597 --> 01:16:51,624
4x6 definitely isn't 26...

2152
01:16:52,012 --> 01:16:54,764
I'm gonna look like
a total idiot on this show.

2153
01:16:54,764 --> 01:16:57,818
They did all the multiplying,
and I was the one who couldn't add.

2154
01:16:57,818 --> 01:17:00,685
I wanted to go on "The Devil's Plan".
What do I do now?

2155
01:17:00,685 --> 01:17:02,748
No one's gonna cast me now.
That's what I was thinking.

2156
01:17:02,748 --> 01:17:05,119
I'm not blaming anyone, but…

2157
01:17:05,119 --> 01:17:08,261
I think DAWN had a really bad headache.

2158
01:17:08,929 --> 01:17:11,197
If we failed because of me,

2159
01:17:11,679 --> 01:17:14,376
the person who made me fail was Lee Teuk.

2160
01:17:14,376 --> 01:17:16,434
Lee Teuk just needed to focus on his part.

2161
01:17:16,434 --> 01:17:17,238
"What is it?"
"The tens place!"

2162
01:17:18,157 --> 01:17:20,621
[Booming voice]
4, 8, 9!! 4, 8, 9!! 3x8 is?

2163
01:17:20,621 --> 01:17:22,495
[Intimidated]
3x8=24!

2164
01:17:22,495 --> 01:17:23,544
3x8=24!

2165
01:17:23,544 --> 01:17:25,779
No! I got them pumped up instead!

2166
01:17:25,779 --> 01:17:27,129
6x8!

2167
01:17:27,129 --> 01:17:28,615
Get it together!!

2168
01:17:28,615 --> 01:17:30,300
That's just an excuse.

2169
01:17:30,784 --> 01:17:32,819
We just couldn't do the math.

2170
01:17:32,819 --> 01:17:35,722
Lee Teuk just kept shouting,
"What is it? What is it?" next to me,

2171
01:17:35,722 --> 01:17:37,691
and I suddenly got so confused.

2172
01:17:37,691 --> 01:17:41,569
I kept thinking,
"Man, I wish he'd just be quiet."

2173
01:17:43,209 --> 01:17:44,297
I'm hitting the slate!

2174
01:17:44,297 --> 01:17:45,799
1, 2, 3!

2175
01:17:47,267 --> 01:17:49,336
[Time to say goodbye now]
Great job! Great job, everyone!

2176
01:17:49,336 --> 01:17:51,338
It's a shame. Like, it would've been nice

2177
01:17:51,338 --> 01:17:55,175
if it ended with us all shouting,
"Success! Whoo!"

2178
01:17:55,175 --> 01:17:57,175
[Regrets]
Such a shame.

2179
01:17:57,644 --> 01:18:00,047
It wasn't important
whether we took the bus or the plane,

2180
01:18:00,047 --> 01:18:04,284
it just would've been great
if we wrapped up with cheering.

2181
01:18:04,284 --> 01:18:05,052
This is fun!

2182
01:18:05,052 --> 01:18:06,353
It really is fun!

2183
01:18:06,353 --> 01:18:09,648
Is 15 minutes always this fast?
Why'd it go so fast?

2184
01:18:10,724 --> 01:18:12,392
The boat as well…

2185
01:18:12,392 --> 01:18:14,574
Going back feels so much faster
than when we headed out.

2186
01:18:14,574 --> 01:18:16,906
I think so too.
The wind is blowing nicely too.

2187
01:18:17,898 --> 01:18:20,691
The journey back usually feels faster,
no matter what it is.

2188
01:18:23,210 --> 01:18:25,792
[That strangely long first day of the trip]
When I saw the Pyramids I'd only seen

2189
01:18:25,792 --> 01:18:27,565
in books as a kid right before my eyes,

2190
01:18:27,565 --> 01:18:29,518
"So, those are the Pyramids!"

2191
01:18:31,140 --> 01:18:33,287
[And the ever-changing fate every day]
It felt like the clouds were hugging me.

2192
01:18:33,287 --> 01:18:34,882
How long do we have
to stay as paupers?

2193
01:18:34,882 --> 01:18:36,766
I'm going to be a prince today.

2194
01:18:36,766 --> 01:18:39,395
[Standing somewhere between hardship and romance]
That night was the absolute worst of the worst.

2195
01:18:39,395 --> 01:18:41,584
My mouth has no saliva left,
but I'm just gonna sleep.

2196
01:18:41,584 --> 01:18:43,892
[Just laughing together]
Me too.

2197
01:18:43,892 --> 01:18:48,054
I think this is the most
memorable moment of this trip.

2198
01:18:48,601 --> 01:18:51,340
[A week that flew by in a flash]
It's truly mystical.

2199
01:18:51,340 --> 01:18:52,799
It's so beautiful.

2200
01:18:52,799 --> 01:18:55,869
After traveling together for almost a week,

2201
01:18:55,869 --> 01:18:58,639
we got to know each other
and grew closer together.

2202
01:18:58,639 --> 01:19:01,441
The thought "I'm sad that I'm a pauper"

2203
01:19:01,441 --> 01:19:04,820
didn't matter after the first day.

2204
01:19:05,706 --> 01:19:09,668
It just felt like we were on a fun trip together,
so I really enjoyed it.

2205
01:19:12,343 --> 01:19:15,488
[And]

2206
01:19:15,488 --> 01:19:19,116
[a shy reflection of the trip]

2207
01:19:19,793 --> 01:19:22,891
After traveling…
It's really fascinating, because…

2208
01:19:22,891 --> 01:19:24,226
[What I'm left with]
Honestly, Egypt was really great,

2209
01:19:24,226 --> 01:19:25,456
["These people"]
but I feel like I gained people,

2210
01:19:25,456 --> 01:19:27,568
and I really loved that.

2211
01:19:27,568 --> 01:19:30,704
Before we departed,
I was actually really worried,

2212
01:19:30,704 --> 01:19:37,110
because it's basically
my first time traveling with friends.

2213
01:19:37,110 --> 01:19:39,313
[With their first-ever travel mates,]
A totally weird combo.

2214
01:19:39,313 --> 01:19:41,548
[they threw awkward questions to each other]
You're really strong! Are you still working out?

2215
01:19:41,548 --> 01:19:43,250
No, no.

2216
01:19:43,250 --> 01:19:47,254
I really tried hard to get close
and thought a lot about it.

2217
01:19:47,254 --> 01:19:50,087
[Making those worries pointless]
The older members made everything so comfortable.

2218
01:19:50,087 --> 01:19:52,993
[we blended so perfectly together]
The younger guys were so nice too.

2219
01:19:54,241 --> 01:19:56,184
[While solo trips are great,]
Traveling is honestly

2220
01:19:56,184 --> 01:19:59,603
[it was way better together]
double the fun when you do it with others.

2221
01:20:00,767 --> 01:20:03,880
I actually like getting lost.

2222
01:20:03,880 --> 01:20:08,475
I'm the type who's fine with detours
as long as there's a destination.

2223
01:20:08,475 --> 01:20:11,051
And on this trip, we took a lot of detours.

2224
01:20:11,051 --> 01:20:12,678
(Throbbing headache)

2225
01:20:13,213 --> 01:20:14,866
(A serious detour)
I shouldn't have eaten that ramyeon…

2226
01:20:14,866 --> 01:20:16,557
Ugh! I'm so annoyed!

2227
01:20:17,132 --> 01:20:20,236
[But even after taking the long way around
or ending up as paupers again,]

2228
01:20:20,821 --> 01:20:22,222
It's okay.

2229
01:20:22,222 --> 01:20:25,008
It's fine, even if we take a detour.

2230
01:20:25,008 --> 01:20:26,322
[What this trip left behind,]
I think it's going to

2231
01:20:26,322 --> 01:20:28,754
["A trip that's worth all the detours"]
stay in my memories. I had so much fun.

2232
01:20:28,754 --> 01:20:30,254
I had so much fun!

2233
01:20:30,254 --> 01:20:33,104
It was hard, and we suffered together,

2234
01:20:33,104 --> 01:20:37,294
but because we suffered together,
I think it made us closer faster.

2235
01:20:37,294 --> 01:20:39,713
[Even when dumped in the middle of a harsh desert]
Just how far…

2236
01:20:39,713 --> 01:20:41,981
Can people see where we are?

2237
01:20:42,543 --> 01:20:45,422
[The first night lying side-by-side stargazing]
Wow! I can see the stars!

2238
01:20:45,422 --> 01:20:46,307
Whoa, this is crazy!

2239
01:20:46,307 --> 01:20:48,916
[When we're together, even hardships turn romantic]
I really love this moment now.

2240
01:20:48,916 --> 01:20:51,210
This is what romance is.

2241
01:20:51,685 --> 01:20:54,439
Because I had gotten
comfortable with the guys,

2242
01:20:54,439 --> 01:20:58,153
I was able to let
my guard down during the filming.

2243
01:20:58,153 --> 01:21:00,367
[What they gained after coming this far]
I think our chemistry

2244
01:21:00,367 --> 01:21:04,016
[A connection they'd love to see again anytime]
as six was incredibly great.

2245
01:21:04,016 --> 01:21:07,063
To me, "happiness" is just…

2246
01:21:07,063 --> 01:21:08,206
Laughing!

2247
01:21:08,774 --> 01:21:12,610
[We laughed a lot, so we must be very happy]
Laughing is happiness, and we laughed a lot in Egypt.

2248
01:21:13,473 --> 01:21:15,275
When else...

2249
01:21:15,275 --> 01:21:16,891
would I get to do something like this?

2250
01:21:16,891 --> 01:21:17,911
I kept thinking,

2251
01:21:17,911 --> 01:21:20,806
"I'm so glad 'ALL or NOTHING'
was my first variety show."

2252
01:21:21,348 --> 01:21:23,211
Personally,

2253
01:21:23,211 --> 01:21:25,001
this will stay with me
for a very long time.

2254
01:21:25,650 --> 01:21:30,471
I feel like I've done so many firsts this year.

2255
01:21:31,124 --> 01:21:32,534
That's great!

2256
01:21:32,534 --> 01:21:34,610
Everything's more fun
when it's your first time!

2257
01:21:34,610 --> 01:21:35,596
Exactly.

2258
01:21:35,596 --> 01:21:38,532
And I think people grow really quickly.

2259
01:21:38,532 --> 01:21:39,366
Definitely.

2260
01:21:39,366 --> 01:21:40,934
[How much you've grown]

2261
01:21:40,934 --> 01:21:43,226
[isn't really important]

2262
01:21:43,950 --> 01:21:46,328
[Now,]

2263
01:21:47,140 --> 01:21:48,909
[with the friends we met in this unfamiliar place,]
I think I learned what traveling is all about.

2264
01:21:48,909 --> 01:21:52,179
Oh, so this is how you're supposed to travel!

2265
01:21:52,179 --> 01:21:56,482
[we are heading back with great memories]

2266
01:21:56,482 --> 01:21:57,754
This is fun!

2267
01:21:58,151 --> 01:22:01,290
"ALL or NOTHING". Paupers and Princes.

2268
01:22:01,290 --> 01:22:02,856
Season 2!

2269
01:22:02,856 --> 01:22:03,891
Look forward to it!

2270
01:22:03,891 --> 01:22:06,643
(Peace)

2271
01:22:08,476 --> 01:22:08,877
1!
2!

2272
01:22:09,312 --> 01:22:10,311
3!

2273
01:22:10,311 --> 01:22:14,006
[It's now time to bring this journey to an end]

2274
01:22:14,501 --> 01:22:16,003
Great job, everyone!

2275
01:22:17,070 --> 01:22:19,637
Ohh… Thank you for all your hard work!

2276
01:22:19,637 --> 01:22:22,431
[Though this bizarre trip is over,]
1, 2, 3!

2277
01:22:23,423 --> 01:22:27,495
[we're heading back to where it all began]

2278
01:22:27,495 --> 01:22:29,038
Save me, please.

2279
01:22:29,038 --> 01:22:30,984
[After failing the mission,
they go on the 7-hour bus ride]

2280
01:22:30,984 --> 01:22:33,695
I really became a pauper today…

2281
01:22:34,621 --> 01:22:35,556
[Saying goodbye now feels bittersweet]
This is crazy.

2282
01:22:35,556 --> 01:22:39,299
We're still filming "ALL or NOTHING".

2283
01:22:39,299 --> 01:22:43,351
[But we look forward
to the day we meet again]

2284
01:22:43,912 --> 01:22:50,019
[Mountains may never meet,
but people always will]

2285
01:23:50,325 --> 01:23:53,634
[Thank you to everyone
who tuned in to "ALL or NOTHING"]
